s: disarmament, human rights, international law and peacekeeping.” Codes of Ethics Online Project (Center for the Study of Ethics in the Professions at Illinois Institute of Technology) http://lawpac.colorado.edu/record=b264885 This database of over 850 professional codes has been updated regularly since 1996. The codes are easily searched by subject categories. Included are early versions of codes of ethics of some organizations for convenient historical research. A literature review, an introduction to the codes, and a User Guide are included.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited NationsvBibliography. 0aLegal research.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075767 0aInternational law & organizations 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aInternational / multinational 6aResearch guide (web)40uhttps://research.un.org/en/docs413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261027130804/https://research.un.org/en/docszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.423Comparable current resource: GlobaLex: Researching the United Nations Documentsuhttps://www.nyulawglobal.org/globalex/UN_Resources_Research_Tools1.html423Comparable current resource, archived version: GlobaLex: Researching the United Nations Documentsuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260520075253/https://www.nyulawglobal.org/globalex/UN_Resources_Research_Tools1.htmlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02485nai a22003737i wotm1998-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nmu|| w o    s0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)44506202  an-us---00aTribal Law Journal.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aTribal Law Journal (University of New Mexico School of Law) 1a[Albuquerque, New Mexico] :bUniversity of New Mexico School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aco