onal 5aFormer Yugoslavia 6aOrganization website 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110261722 aInternational Tribunal for the Prosecution of Persons Responsible for Serious Violations of International Humanitarian Law Committed in the Territory of the Former Yugoslavia since 1991,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n9409386440uhttps://www.icty.org/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261027192227/https://www.icty.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02198nai a22003137i 4500001001200000005001700012006001900029007001500048008004100063035002000104043001200124245004200136264005000178300002200228336002600250337002600276338003600302500008800338500008100426500023800507506006500745520049200810588015401302650010301456653003701559655008901596856004201685856015701727wotm1998-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)41216759  an-us---00aIntroduction to Basic Legal Citation. 1a[Ithaca, N.Y.] :bLegal Information Institute  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1998).  aFeatured between 2000-12 and 2002-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aPresents information on legal citation, provided by Peter W. Martin. Discusses the purposes of legal citation and the general types of citation rules. Highlights how to cite cases, constitutions, regulations, arbitrations, rules of evidence, law journal writing, and documents from earlier stages of a case. Contains example citations, as well as abbreviations and omissions used in citations. Offers information on underlining in citations and text.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCitation of legal authoritieszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100795 0aLegal research & reference tools 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402610940uhttps://www.law.cornell.edu/citation/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261104171312/https://www.law.cornell.edu/citation/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03323nai a22003737i wotm1998-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuctu|| d o    |0    2eng d00aSearch JAKE. 1a[New Haven, Connecticut] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1998).  aFeatured between 2000-11 and 2002-03 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aJAKE is a free website developed at Yale Medical Library that allows you to search for a journal to see which databases index it and/or include the full-text. You can search by journal title; database title; ISSN; or citation to a specific article using journal title, volumes, issue, page and year. This site is unique in giving us a way to keep current on the constantly changing nature of serials in electronic format. There are roughly 23,000 journals included in 200 databases, and many are full-text.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPeriodicalsvIndexesvDatabases. 0aGeneral reference (not law-specific) 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aIndexes.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026112403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20000303105141/http://jake.med.yale.edu/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.423About this resource (not the resource itself): Review of jake, C&RL News 'Internet Reviews' (Sara Amato, March 2000)uhttps://crln.acrl.org/index.php/crlnews/article/view/19247/22405423About this resource (not the resource itself), archived version: Review of jake, C&RL News 'Internet Reviews' (Sara Amato, March 2000)uhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261110210328/https://crln.acrl.org/index.php/crlnews/article/view/19247/22405zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.423About this resource (not the resource itself): Wikipedia: Jointly Administered Knowledge Environmentuhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jointly_Administered_Knowledge_Environment423About this resource (not the resource itself), archived version: Wikipedia: Jointly Administered Knowledge Environmentuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260211055329/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jointly_Administered_Knowledge_EnvironmentzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02367nai a22003377i wotm1998-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999wiu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)4427539400aAll That JAS :bJournal Abbreviation Sources. 1a[Madison, Wisconsin] :bUniversity of Wisconsin-Madison Libraries  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1998).  aFeatured between 2000-10 and 2002-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site is a registry of Web resources that list or provide access to the full title of journal abbreviations or other types of abbreviated publication titles (e.g., conference proceedings titles). It includes “Bluebook Abbreviations of Law Review Titles” from the University of Washington, School of Law, Marian Gould Gallagher Law Library.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPeriodicalsxAbbreviations of titles.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2003003675 0aLawxAbbreviations.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075120 0aLegal research & reference tools 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 7aAbbreviation dictionaries.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20250261262 aUniversity of Wisconsin--Madison,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8012627740uhttps://search.library.wisc.edu/database/UWI11733413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260520224601/https://search.library.wisc.edu/database/UWI11733zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02589nai a22003497i wotm1999-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    |0    2eng d00aReference Guide to the Geneva Conventions.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aReference Guide to the Geneva Conventions / Maria Trombley. (Society of Professional Journalists) 1a[Ithaca, N.Y.] :bSociety of Professional Journalists/LII  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2004-06 and 2004-07 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site is the online version of the Journalist’s Guide to the Geneva Conventions, and provides access to the four Geneva Conventions, the two Protocols of 1977, as well as the history of the Conventions. It also includes links to other treaties on human rights, weapons, and genocide, as well as an alphabetical index that provides references to specific convention text relevant to particular topics.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aHumanitarian law.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh99002222 0aWar victimsxLegal status, laws, etc.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85145230 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational criminal law & transitional justice 0aInternational / multinational 7aTreaties.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026707 7aGuidebooks.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402610840uhttps://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/geneva_conventions_and_their_additional_protocols413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261030085329/https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/geneva_conventions_and_their_additional_protocolszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02571nai a22003617i wotm1999-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuutnu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aFirst Amendment Center. 1a[Nashville, Tenn.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured 2004-05 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aContinued by a successor resource (linked below).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThe First Amendment Center serves as a forum for the study and exploration of free-expression issues, including freedom of speech, of the press and of religion, the right to assemble and petition the government. The Center, with offices at Vanderbilt University in Nashville, Tenn., and Arlington, Va., is an operating program of the Freedom Forum and is associated with the Newseum.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aFreedom of speechzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008103692 0aFreedom of the presszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008104079 0aFreedom of religionzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008104095 0aAssembly, Right ofzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009116065 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website00tFree Speech Center / First Amendment Encyclopedia (MTSU)423Successor resource: Free Speech Center / First Amendment Encyclopedia (MTSU)uhttps://firstamendment.mtsu.edu/article/first-amendment-center/423Successor resource, archived version: Free Speech Center / First Amendment Encyclopedia (MTSU)uhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260717144628/https://firstamendment.mtsu.edu/article/first-amendment-center/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02853nai a22004217i wotm1999-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)44280903  an-us---00aAdmiralty and Maritime Law Guide. 1a[Richmond, Virginia] :bUniversity of Richmond School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2004-04 and 2004-05 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Admiralty and Maritime Law Guide includes over 1,500 annotated links to admiralty law resources on the Internet and a growing database of admiralty case digests, opinions and international maritime conventions. The emphasis is on the law of the United States and the focus is on Internet resources that can be used in an effective and practical manner by admiralty attorneys and maritime professionals.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAdmiraltyzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100648 0aMaritime lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008107415 0aAdmiralty.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85000930 0aMaritime law.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85081308 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 0aInternational law & organizations 0aUnited States (federal) 0aInternational / multinational 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110261722 aUniversity of Richmond.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200108852040uhttps://law-richmond.libguides.com/c.php?g=129499&p=846093413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260825003210/https://law-richmond.libguides.com/c.php?g=129499&p=846093zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03242nai a22004217i wotm1999-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)53092579  aa-iq---00aTransitional Justice in Post-Saddam Iraq & Iraqi Jurists' Association.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aTransitional Justice in Post-saddam Iraq: The Road to Re-establishing Rule of Law and Restoring Civil Society: A Blueprint 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bWorking Group on Transitional Justice in Iraq  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2004-03 and 2004-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis report, dated March 2003, is the product of the Working Group on Transitional Justice of the Future of Iraq Project (Working Group), which worked in cooperation with the Iraqi Jurists’Association. Comprised primarily of prominent former Iraqi judges, lawyers and law professors, the Working Group embarked on this project in July 2002 in consultation with international experts in the areas of international criminal law, truth and reconciliation, post-conflict justice and military reform. The resulting Transitional Justice Plan is aimed at transforming an unstable and chaotic state, caused by a dictatorship with a legacy of gross human rights abuses, to a democratic pluralistic system which respects the rule of law.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aHussein, Saddam,d1937-2006.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n810245711http://isni.org/isni/0000000139974396 0aLaw reformzIraq. 0aJustice, Administration ofzIraq. 0aHuman rightszIraq.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008122080 0aIraqxPolitics and governmenty1991-2003.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98007501 0aInternational criminal law & transitional justice 0aHuman rights 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aIraq 6aReport or study (single document)40uhttps://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-S-PURL-LPS36686/pdf/GOVPUB-S-PURL-LPS36686.pdf413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260718004827/https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-S-PURL-LPS36686/pdf/GOVPUB-S-PURL-LPS36686.pdfzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02947nai a22003737i wotm1999-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)52175638  an-us---00aNational Governors' Association Online. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bNational Governors' Association  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2004-02 and 2004-03 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site presents information about the National Governors’ Association (NGA), a bipartisan organization for the governors of the U.S. states, the commonwealths of the Northern Mariana Islands and Puerto Rico, and the territories of American Samoa, Guam, and the Virgin Islands. The site includes an overview and history of the organization, which provides a forum for governors to exchange views and experiences. The NGA provides assistance in solving state-focused problems, information on state innovations and practices, and a bipartisan forum for governors to establish, influence, and implement policy on national issues. It posts press releases, along with contact information via mailing and e-mail addresses and telephone numbers. The site also contains a user-friendly comprehensive database of all past and present U.S. governors.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aNational Governors' Association.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780019401http://isni.org/isni/0000000087015125 0aGovernorszUnited StatesxStates. 0aState governmentszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008112230 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aOrganization website2 aNational Governors' Association,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7800194040