110cuuuu9999ctu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)3734254004aThe Avalon Project at Yale Law School :bDocuments in Law, History and Diplomacy. 1a[New Haven, Connecticut] :bYale Law School  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2003-08 and 2003-12 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Avalon Project is dedicated to providing digital document access to primary source materials in the fields of Law, History, Economics, Politics, Diplomacy and Government.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawvSources.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075144 0aPolitical science literaturevSources. 0aUnited StatesxHistoryvSources.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140327 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aInternational law & organizations 0aUnited States (federal) 0aInternational / multinational 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf202202607940uhttps://avalon.law.yale.edu413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261031114003/https://avalon.law.yale.eduzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02584nai a22003617i wotm1999-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || w o    |0    2eng d  ae-gx---ae------04aThe German Law Journal :bReview of Developments in German, European and International Jurisprudence. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bGerman Law Journal  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2003-07 and 2003-11 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe first and only on-line, English-language report on developments in German and European jurisprudence. With regard to both Public Law and Private Law in Germany, as well as European Law, GLJ provides thoughtful, quality reporting while inviting further commentary on and analysis of the issues on which it reports. GLJ’s frequent publication schedule permits the most contemporary coverage. GLJ also provides coverage of German and European Legal Culture, including annoncements of conferences and other events of interest, book reviews, and coverage of appointments to the judiciary.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzGermanyvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106775 0aLawzEuropean Union countriesvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009129114 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aForeign & comparative law 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aGermany 5aEuropean Union 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102635240uhttps://germanlawjournal.com413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029190314/https://germanlawjournal.comzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02430nai a22003737i wotm1999-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999mau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)53937686  ae-gx---00aNuremberg Trials Project.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aWar Crimes Trials at Nuremberg. (Harvard Law School Library) 1a[Cambridge, Mass.] :bHarvard Law School Library  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2003-06 and 2003-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site contains a collection of trial transcripts, briefs, document books, evidence files, and other documents relating to the trial of Nazi military and political leaders of the Third Reich before the International Military Tribunal (IMT) and to trials of other accused war criminals.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aNuremberg War Crime Trials, Nuremberg, Germany, 1946-1949.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85093308 0aInternational criminal law & transitional justice 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aInternational / multinational 6aDigital archive / collection 7aTrial and arbitral proceedings.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110267082 aHarvard Law School.bLibrary,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8323461640uhttps://nuremberg.law.harvard.edu413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261023132754/https://nuremberg.law.harvard.eduzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02853nai a22004097i wotm1999-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)51686551  an-us---00aNational Strategy to Secure Cyberspace. (U.S. Office of the President). 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured between 2003-05 and 2003-09 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“[This] an implementing component of the National Strategy for Homeland Security and is complemented by a National Strategy for the Physical Protection of Critical Infrastructures and Key Assets . The purpose of this document is to engage and empower Americans to secure the portions of cyberspace that they own, operate, control, or with which they interact. Securing cyberspace is a difficult strategic challenge that requires coordinated and focused effort from our entire society, the federal government, state and local governments, the private sector, and the American people.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aComputer crimeszUnited States. 0aNational securityzUnited States. 0aTerrorismxPreventionxGovernment policyzUnited States.