iption based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aParental kidnappingzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010105113 0aCustody of childrenzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100403 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aInternational law & organizations 0aUnited States (federal) 0aInternational / multinational 7aGuidebooks.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261081 aUnited States.bOffice of Juvenile Justice and Delinquency Prevention,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8213161440uhttps://www.ojp.gov/pdffiles1/ojjdp/215476.pdf413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260702135929/https://www.ojp.gov/pdffiles1/ojjdp/215476.pdfzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02478nai a22003857i wotm1999-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)39845641  an-us---04aThe Oyez Project.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aThe Oyez Project, Northwestern University 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bJustia Supreme Court Center  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 1999).  aFeatured 2003-03 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aPresents Oyez Oyez Oyez, a multimedia database about the United States Supreme Court. Includes audio files of oral arguments, abstracts of key constitutional cases, and information on Supreme Court justices. Offers a virtual tour of the U.S. Supreme Court building in Washington, D.C. Lists justices alphabetically and in order of appointment.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States. Supreme Court.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79006848 0aConstitutional lawzUnited StatesvCases.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85139989 0aJudgeszUnited StatesvBiography.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009127943 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102617240uhttps://www.oyez.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20150101093839/https://www.oyez.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02573nai a22003497i wotm2000-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ilu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)5490190900aNorthwestern University Journal of International Human Rights. 1a[Chicago, Ill.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis journal is produced by students at the Northwestern University School of Law. According to the journal’s homepage, the journal “… is dedicated to providing a dynamic new forum for the vigorous discussion of human rights issues of all varieties among scholars of all disciplines and perspectives. Recognizing that a comprehensive examination of international human rights cannot be accomplished based on legal principles alone, the Journal seeks contribution from professionals in all areas, including but not limited to law, business, ethics, political science, economics, religion, and sociology.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aHuman rightsvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008105911 0aInternational lawvPeriodicals. 0aHuman rights 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aInternational / multinational 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263522 aNorthwestern University (Evanston, Ill.). School of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8103993440uhttps://jhr.law.northwestern.edu/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260520230624/https://jhr.law.northwestern.edu/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02067nai a22003617i wotm2000-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    |0    2eng d00aGlobaLex. 1a[New York] :bNew York University School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis website is dedicated to international and foreign law research, and the dissemination of high-level international, foreign, and comparative law research tools.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegal research.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075767 0aInternational lawxResearch. 0aComparative lawxResearch. 0aForeign & comparative law 0aInternational law & organizations 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aInternational / multinational 6aResearch guide (web)2 aNew York University.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8101338140uhttps://www.nyulawglobal.org/globalex413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261106161543/https://www.nyulawglobal.org/globalexzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02048nai a22003257i wotm2000-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuvau|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aCourTopics. 1a[Williamsburg, Virginia] :bNational Center for State Courts  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2005-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThis website is directed towards the state justice community. It contains over 100 court-related topics, which include overviews, research reports, resource guides, frequently asked questions, best practices, and NCSC publications.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCourtszUnited StatesxStates.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85033577 0aCourt administrationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009121326 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aResearch guide (web)2 aNational Center for State Courts,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79129627423About this resource (not the resource itself): Article about CourTopics (JSTOR)uhttps://www.jstor.org/stable/2797716302389nai a22003377i wotm2000-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)95862680200aSanta Clara Journal of International Law. 1a[Santa Clara, California] :bSanta Clara University School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2005-02 and 2005-03 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Santa Clara Journal of International Law hopes to redefine legal journalism by publishing an easily accessible, entirely web-based international law journal composed of rigorous, accessible, and intellectually sound material. Each journal volume contains materials from a diverse representation of international scholars. In addition to the online journal, book reviews and articles are posted on the website. The Journal also hosts an annual symposium at Santa Clara University, School of Law.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aInternational lawvPeriodicals. 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational / multinational 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263522 aUniversity of Santa Clara.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n5006754040uhttps://digitalcommons.law.scu.edu/scujil/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20251221162229/https://digitalcommons.law.scu.edu/scujil/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02399nai a22003257i wotm2000-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ctu|| w o    |0    2eng d00aYale Journal of Law and Technology. 1a[New Haven, Conn.] :bYale University  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2005-01 and 2005-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Yale Journal of Law & Technology (YJoLT) is the first law review in the world to offer its readership a fully interactive environment in which to acquire and disseminate knowledge about the interface between law and technology. Formerly the Yale Symposium on Law & Technology, the Journal not only publishes lectures and written pieces by the diverse and distinguished guests of Yale Law School as well as other scholars, practitioners, and students, it also provides a forum for a robust community discussion of the issues raised in its published pieces.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aTechnology and lawvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009102787 0aInformation technologyxLaw and legislationvPeriodicals. 0aIntellectual property, technology & privacy 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263522 aYale Law School,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8104789440uhttps://yjolt.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261017115706/https://yjolt.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02192nai a22003497i wotm2000-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aGreenLaw.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aGreenlaw : Journal of the Pace Environmental Law Program 1a[White Plains, N.Y.] :bPace University School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2004-12 and 2005-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis journal contains short, quality articles on a wide range of environmental law issues. In addition, it provides summaries of important lectures on environmental law at Pace.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of