nline access2star  aWeb site of the Library’s Harry Blackmun paper collection. Selected materials from the collection, including the oral history video interviews and associated transcript, have been digitized and are available online at this site. A finding aid and selected bibliography on Blackmun are also available.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States. Supreme CourtxHistory. 0aJudgeszUnited StatesvArchives. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aOral histories.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110264312 aLibrary of Congress.bManuscript Division,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7808064240uhttps://findingaids.loc.gov/db/search/xq/searchMfer02.xq?_id=loc.mss.eadmss.ms003030&_faSection=overview&_faSubsection=did&_dmdid=413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250613063706/https://findingaids.loc.gov/db/search/xq/searchMfer02.xq?_id=loc.mss.eadmss.ms003030&_faSection=overview&_faSubsection=did&_dmdid=zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02477nai a22003617i wotm2000-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| d o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aHarmful Error :bInvestigating America's Local Prosecutors. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bCenter for Public Integrity  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2000).  aFeatured between 2004-07 and 2004-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site presents the results of an investigative study of prosecutorial misconduct in the U.S. conducted by the Center for Public Integrity. Sections of the site include Main Findings, Prosecutor Profiles, Analyses, Nationwide Numbers, Updates and Corrections, and a database searching option.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPublic prosecutorszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh96008615 0aProsecutionzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008110109 0aCriminal law & criminal justice 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aReport or study (single document) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aCenter for Public Integrity,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr9401451540uhttps://publicintegrity.org/topics/politics/state-politics/harmful-error/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250402151759/https://publicintegrity.org/topics/politics/state-politics/harmful-error/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02305nai a22003377i wotm2001-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us-dc00aCouncil for Court Excellence. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bCCE  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2001).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site presents basic reference information about the history of the federal courts and the judges who have served on those courts since 1789. It contains six topical links: Judges of the United States Courts; Courts of the Federal Judiciary; Judicial Administration and Organization; Landmark Judicial Legislation; Judicial History News; and a Courthouse Photograph Exhibit. In addition, the site includes links to other internet sites related to the history of the federal judiciary and to history-related publications from the Federal Judicial Center.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aJustice, Administration ofzWashington (D.C.) 0aCourtszWashington (D.C.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009122219 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website40uhttps://www.courtexcellence.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029181842/https://www.courtexcellence.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02672nai a22003857i wotm2001-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999mnu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)6152497700aFrequently-Cited Treaties & Other International Instruments.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aFrequently-cited Treaties and Other International Instruments 1a[Minneapolis, Minn.] :bUniversity of Minnesota Law School  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2001).