istory Research Guides on the Web. 1a[Philadelphia] :bPenn Carey Law School, University of Pennsylvania  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2001).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aCompilation of online legislative history research guides for most of the 50 statescLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegislative historieszUnited StatesxStates. 0aLegal researchzUnited StatesxStates. 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 6aResearch guide (web)40uhttps://law.upenn.libguides.com/c.php?g=279289&p=8327276413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260825003225/https://law.upenn.libguides.com/c.php?g=279289&p=8327276zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02597nai a22003737i wotm2001-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)62162727  an-us---00aSunshine Week. 1a[Arlington, Va.] :bSociety of Professional Journalists  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2001).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“Sunshine Week” is an open-government initiative made up of newspaper editors, broadcasters, bloggers, legislators, librarians, and civic groups. In addition to background information on the Sunshine Week Project and its supporters and coordinators, the site provides access to other materials on open access, including a Toolkit section, tips for writing about open government, and advice on conducting a Freedom of Information audit and how to make requests under the Freedom of Information Act. The site also links to numerous news stories and editorials on open access.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPublic meetingszUnited States. 0aPublic recordszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008110033 0aGovernment informationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008105358 0aFreedom of informationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008103817 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website40uhttps://sunshineweek.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029064027/https://sunshineweek.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03016nai a22003977i wotm2001-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)60660375  an-us---00aEFF :bLegal Guide for Bloggers. 1a[San Francisco] :bElectronic Frontier Foundation  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2001).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-02 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe “EFF” in “EFF : legal guide for bloggers” stands for the Electronic Frontier Foundation. According to the homepage of the Legal guide for bloggers, EFF “… is a non-profit civil liberties organization working in the public interest to protect privacy, free expression, and access to public resources and information online, as well as to promote responsibility in new media.” The Legal guide for bloggers site contains a collection of frequently asked questions (FAQs) for bloggers about their legal rights. Topics include intellectual property, online defamation law, section 230 (of the Communication Decency Act of 1996) protections, and privacy. Also includes FAQs for bloggers as journalists on reporter’s privilege and media access, and FAQs relating to election and labor laws.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aBlogsxLaw and legislationzUnited States. 0aWeb publishingzUnited States. 0aFreedom of information.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85051702 0aFreedom of speech.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85051707 0aIntellectual property, technology & privacy 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 7aGuidebooks.2lcgft0htt