ng the story of the Watergate scandal. Also included are materials used for Washington Post articles and the books “All the President’s Men” and “The Final Days.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aWatergate Affair, 1972-1974.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85145735 0aWatergate Affair, 1972-1974xArchival resources. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20220260792 aUniversity of Texas at Austin,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7902332340uhttps://research.hrc.utexas.edu/fasearch/findingAid.cfm?eadid=00365413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260926064128/https://research.hrc.utexas.edu/fasearch/findingAid.cfm?eadid=00365zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02582nai a22003497i wotm2002-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999pau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)3956494300aJuristnews.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aJurist 1a[Pittsburgh, Pa.] :bJurist/University of Pittsburgh  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the JURIST website, it “…is a Web-based legal news and real-time legal research service powered by a mostly-volunteer team of over 30 part-time law student reporters, editors, and Web developers led by law professor Bernard Hibbitts at the University of Pittsburgh School of Law in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA. JURIST is produced as a public service for the continuing legal education of its readers and law student staffers, and uses the latest Internet technology to track important legal news stories and materials and present them rapidly, objectively and intelligibly in an accessible, ad-free format.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawxStudy and teaching.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075145 0aLaw.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075119 0aLegal research & reference tools 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261392 aUniversity of Pittsburgh.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8106260740uhttps://www.jurist.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261017124814/https://www.jurist.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02103nai a22003257i wotm2002-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)3265209900aD-Lib Magazine. 1a[Reston, Va.] :bCorporation for National Research Initiatives  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“D-Lib Magazine is a solely electronic publication with a primary focus on digital library research and development, including but not limited to new technologies, applications, and contextual social and economic issues.”–About D-Lib MagazinecLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aDigital librariesvPeriodicals. 0aInformation technologyvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008104637 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261392 aCorporation for National Research Initiatives,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n9206871940uhttps://www.dlib.org/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260101005456/https://www.dlib.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02515nai a22003857i wotm2002-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)48409594  an-us---00aE :bEnvironmental Defense. 1a[New York] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aWeb site of the Environmental Defense, a not-for-profit environmental advocacy organization. Offers campaigns and action items for activists, resources for journalists and researchers, and programs which bring together experts in science, law and economics to tackle complex environmental issuescLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aEnvironmental Defense (Organization)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no000730661http://isni.org/isni/0000000096952743 0aEnvironmental lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009103157 0aEnvironmental protectionzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85044209 0aEnvironmentalismzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007004672 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aEnvironmental Defense Fund,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7900556140uhttps://www.edf.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029181414/https://www.edf.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02293nai a22003377i wotm2002-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| d o    |0    2eng d00aEarthTrends :bThe Environmental Information Portal. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bLibrary of Congress  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAn environmental information portal for researching global topics, such as water resources, climate and atmosphere, population and health, energy resources, and agriculture and food. Allows users to gather information from the searchable database, display data tables, view country profiles, or select maps with global, regional, and country-level environmental informationcLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aEnvironmental indicatorsvDatabases. 0aNatural resourcesvStatistics. 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aInternational / multinational 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261812 aWorld Resources Institute,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8404227940uhttps://www.loc.gov/item/2002604985/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260504203413/https://www.loc.gov/item/2002604985/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02786nai a22003617i wotm2002-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)6216235500aFIELD :bFoundation for International Environmental Law and Development. 1a[London] :bFoundation for International Environmental Law and Development  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aFounded in 1989 by a small group of international lawyers, the Foundation for International Environmental Law and Development is an organization which offers its advice and assistance to governments, inter-governmental entities and non-governmental organizations world-wide. The website provides papers and publications, including Explanatory Guides, International Environmental Law Papers, EU Environmental Law Papers, and other relevant materials. The site also provides overviews of its current and past projects dealing with issues such as biodiversity, marine resources, climate change, and strengthening capacitycLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aFoundation for International Environmental Law and Development.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no920197121http://isni.org/isni/0000000404247991 0aEnvironmental law, International.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85044188 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website2 aFoundation for International Environmental Law and Development,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9201971240uhttp://www.field.org.uk413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20130112220240/http://www.field.org.ukzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02602nai a22003737i wotm2002-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ctu|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)6869485600aRepresenting Children Worldwide. 1a[New Haven, Conn.] :bYale Law School  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aRepresenting Children Worldwide is a research project which compiles information and resources on how children’s voices are heard in child protective proceedings around the country and around the world in the year 2005. The website provides a summary of the practices of the 194 signatories to the United Nations Convention on the Rights of a Child (UNCRC) with respect to this question, as well as background information on the jurisdiction’s child protective practices and web resources and contact information for further research in this fieldcLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aChildrenxLegal status, laws, etc.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85023456 0aLegal assistance to children.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075722 0aChildren's rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85023773 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aHuman rights 0aForeign & comparative law 0aInternational / multinational 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aYale Law School,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8104789440uhttps://rcw.law.yale.edu413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260905190828/https://rcw.law.yale.eduzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02293nai a22003497i wotm2002-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)6869443200aInternational Law Commission. 1a[New York] :bUnited Nations General Assembly  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe website provides information about the work and history of the Commission. In the “Researching the work of the Commission” section, the following materials are included: a research guide, topics, texts and instruments, documentation, publications and a search page. The publications area also includes the full text of the Commission’s yearbookscLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aInternational law.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85067417 0aInternational lawxCodification.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85067419 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website2 aUnited Nations.bInternational Law Commission,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8106163840uhttps://legal.un.org/ilc/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261101170801/https://legal.un.org/ilc/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02197nai a22003857i wotm2002-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu99