  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aContinued by a successor resource (linked below).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThe Municipal codes web library provides links to municipal and county codes from various states published through LexisNexis Municipal Codes Publishing and Ordlink Services.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aOrdinances, MunicipalzUnited States. 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 7aStatutes and codes.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110266112 aLexisNexis (Firm),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9503678500tMunicode Library403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20091021184153/http://municipalcodes.lexisnexis.comzArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.423Successor resource: Municode Libraryuhttps://library.municode.com/423Successor resource, archived version: Municode Libraryuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261006225014/https://library.municode.com/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03445nai a22003977i wotm2002-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| d o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)18255272300aGlobal Legal Information Network :bGLIN.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aGlobal Legal Information Network 1aWashington, D.C :bLaw Library of Congress  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aTitle, publication and subject data from the University of Hawaiʻi Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aGLIN is a database of laws, regulations, and other complementary legal sources. The documents included in the database are contributed by the governments of the member nations from the original official texts which are deposited, by agreement of the members, in a server at the Library of Congress, sponsored by the Law Library of Congress. The basic elements of this database are: (1) full texts of the documents in the official language of the country of origin; (2) summaries or abstracts in English; and (3) an English thesaurus. GLIN data fields in the database include country/entity, GLIN thesaurus, title, date of issuance, date of publication, instrument class, instrument number, language, and others. The summaries or abstracts are linked electronically to the corresponding full texts. Access to the contents of the database is at two levels: guests have access to the summaries and citations to laws; members and associate members can access the full content of the database upon issuance of passwords. Inquiries about GLIN can be addressed to glincen@loc.gov.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawvDatabases. 0aGazettesvDatabases. 0aForeign & comparative law 0aInternational / multinational 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aStatutes and codes.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110266112 aLaw Library of Congress (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n9104313700tGuide to Law Online (Nations)423Successor resource: Guide to Law Online (Nations)uhttps://www.loc.gov/research-centers/law-library-of-congress/researcher-resources/guide-to-law-online/423Successor resource: Global Legal Monitoruhttps://www.loc.gov/collections/global-legal-monitor/423Successor resource, archived version: Global Legal Monitoruhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261028010835/https://www.loc.gov/collections/global-legal-monitor/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.05031nai a22005057i wotm2002-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)61433340  an-us---00aSenate Committee on the Judiciary :bSupreme Court Nomination Hearings. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bGovInfo  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site contains PDF files of all Senate Judiciary Committee hearings on *successful* Supreme Court nominations from the Rehnquist-Powell hearings in 1971 to the Roberts hearings in 2005. The older prints have been both scanned and OCR’ed, so they are searchable, as well as amenable to copy and paste functions. Specifically, the transcripts include the hearings on the Associate Justice of the Supreme Court nominations of William H. Rehnquist, Lewis F. Powell, John Paul Stevens, Sandra Day O’Connor, Antonin Scalia, Anthony M. Kennedy, David H. Souter, Clarence Thomas, Ruth Bader Ginsburg and Stephen G. Breyer; Hearing on the Nomination of Justice William H. Rehnquist to be Chief Justice of the United States; Hearing on the Nomination of John G. Roberts, Jr. to be Chief Justice of the United States. Presumably, the Alito hearing will be added when the Committee print is published.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aRehnquist, William H.,d1924-20050http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8602300998c2f464d-f34e-48fd-8f80-a101a4ab2b4a1http://isni.org/isni/000000008258576X10aPowell, Lewis F.,cJr.,d1907-19980http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8784369893e8caa27-ae00-4a0d-90bf-e55388aaa67e1http://isni.org/isni/000000011475631710aStevens, John Paul,d1920-20190http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n881170359e6eb0fcf-6987-4494-b234-11314b5efc9e1http://isni.org/isni/000000012120673510aO'Connor, Sandra Day,d1930-20230http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n811236939cba70258-7bff-4d09-9106-970d457fdd861http://isni.org/isni/000000010939098X10aScalia, Antonin,d1936-20160http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n853512119c0863af8-a7a9-4f2d-81a1-8313cc0f17e31http://isni.org/isni/000000011461922410aKennedy, Anthony M.,d1936-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8807738493558e4a8-f82a-40a5-a2c5-13fa72b671891http://isni.org/isni/000000007886102010aSouter, David H.,d1939-20250http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no900225469528ab4fa-7777-4cd3-93f4-2e37c2fd9fee1http://isni.org/isni/000000038560894910aThomas, Clarence,d1948-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82137324914e81112-49dc-4812-bbab-c0fc90a148bd1http://isni.org/isni/000000043481523210aGinsburg, Ruth Bader,d1933-20200http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n50029918904091317-e1bd-44b2-a785-f8158328b2361http://isni.org/isni/000000008158099110aBreyer, Stephen G.,d1938-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n791264629636bc891-5510-47e2-be2d-e02fecb7c0b21http://isni.org/isni/000000010931850710aRoberts, John G.,cJr.,d1955-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9902042697cc77192-47ef-4060-a81d-333f76e537241http://isni.org/isni/000000004662558410aUnited States.bSupreme CourtxOfficials and employeesxNomination and appointment. 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aUnited States (federal) 7aLegislative materials.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263621 aUnited States.bGovernment Publishing Office,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20150025031 aUnited States.bCongress.bSenate.bCommittee on the Judiciary,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8220958740uhttps://www.govinfo.gov/collection/supreme-court-nomination-hearings413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260703235249/https://www.govinfo.gov/collection/supreme-court-nomination-hearingszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02572nai a22003857i wotm2002-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)62414885  an-us---00aAlliance for Justice. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bAlliance for Justice  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2002).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe “Alliance for justice” works to promote a fair and independent judiciary and strengthen public interest advocacy. Its website contains extensive information about its political activities and membership functions. In addition, the “Research and Publications” section provides the full text of reports (in PDF) on judicial nominations and select bills and legislation, and other publications aimed at non-profit and foundation organizers.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aAlliance for Justice.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n881583161http://isni.org/isni/0000000096170602 0aJustice, Administration ofzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008122526 0aPublic interest lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010107990 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aAlliance for Justice,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8815831640uhttps://afj.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261019130357/https://afj.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02576nai a22003857i wotm2003-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)47124380  an-us---00aResearching U.S. Treaties and Agreements. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aResearching U.S. treaties and agreements , a guide by Marci Hoffman available on the LLRX (Law Library Resource Xchange) website. Marci has created an extensive guide to researching multilaterial and bilateral agreements to which the United States is a signatory. Topics include: locating and updating treaties; indexes to treaty collections; treaty research online; status information; implementation and interpretation; drafting of treaties; and bilateral treaties outside of the U.S.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aTreatiesxResearchxMethodology. 0aUnited StatesxForeign relationsvTreatiesvBibliography. 0aUnited StatesxForeign relationsvTreatiesxComputer network resourcesvDirectories. 0aInternational law & organizations 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aUnited States (federal) 0aInternational / multinational 6aResearch guide (web)40uhttps://www.llrx.com/2001/05/features-researching-u-s-treaties-and-agreements/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260809105831/https://www.llrx.com/2001/05/features-researching-u-s-treaties-and-agreements/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03891nai a22003857i wotm2003-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999aru|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)56104834  an-us---04aThe National Agricultural Law Center. 1a[Fayetteville, Ark.] :bUniversity of Arkansas School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003, 2019).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aFeatured between 2019-05 and 2019-09 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Center is part of the University of Arkansas School of Law, and the site is a premier source for information and scholarly research on agricultural and food law. The site features “Reading Rooms” that provide in-depth coverage on specific agricultural and food subjects, which include topical background information, statutes, regulations, judicial and administrative decisions, Center publications, and online reference sources. The National AgLaw Reporter, a regularly updated electronic newsletter, provides current news, case summaries, regulatory changes, and administrative decisions. United States Farm Bills offers the full text of the nation’s farm bills from 1933 to the present, along with links to legislative history, analysis, and background resources. A quarterly-updated and searchable AgLaw Bibliography provides scholarly sources on 48 agricultural and food law topics.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aThe National Agricultural Law Center established in 1987 at the University of Arkansas serves as the nation’s leading source of agricultural and food law research and information. The Center is a federally funded and a nonpartisan entity. The operation of the Center is in conjunction with the United States National Agricultural Library. The Center’s website is the primary means of disseminating its agricultural and food law research and information products. The Center is part of Agricultural Research Service of the United States Department of Agricultural (USDA) and is the only institution of its kind in the United States. The Center serve the nation’s vast agricultural community. Their clientele includes attorneys, farmers, federal and state policymakers, extension personnel, academics, students, and consumers.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAgricultural laws and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85002351 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aUniversity of Arkansas, Fayetteville.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8207201740uhttps://nationalaglawcenter.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029152526/https://nationalaglawcenter.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02693nai a22003617i wotm2003-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999mnu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)71837884  an-us---00aFLAG :bFarmers' Legal Action Group, Incorporated. 1a[Saint Paul, Minnesota] :bFarmers' Legal Action Group  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aFLAG is a nonprofit law center dedicated to providing legal services to family farmers and their rural communities in order to help keep family farmers on the land. FLAG focuses on areas such as factory farms, biotechnology, disaster assistance, and sustainable and organic agriculture. The FLAG main page provides news, press releases, Farm Service Agency (FSA) administrative notices, and related articles. Summaries of significant decisions in agricultural law court cases are published in the Farmers’ Legal Action Report. Visitors to FLAG’s page may read the Group’s comments to federal rules and highlights of the Federal Register. FLAG’s amicus briefs are also available on the site.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aFamily farmsxLaw and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008120197 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aFarmers' Legal Action Group,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9504589440uhttp://www.flaginc.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029121958/http://www.flaginc.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02635nai a22004337i wotm2003-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999txu|| w o    |0    2eng d  ae-fr---ae-gx---ae-it---00aForeign Law Translations. 1a[Austin, Texas] :bUniversity of Texas at Austin School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aContaining nearly 1,000 translated judicial decisions and statutes, this website is a resource for French, German, Italian, Austrian and Israeli legal materials in the fields of constitutional, administrative, contract and tort law.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aComparative law.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85029299 0aLawzFrance.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075160 0aLawzGermany.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075162 0aLawzItaly.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075172 0aForeign & comparative law 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aFrance 5aGermany 5aItaly 5aAustria 5aIsrael 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026172 7aStatutes and codes.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110266112 aUniversity of Texas at Austin.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8215921640uhttps://law.utexas.edu/transnational/foreign-law-translations/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20251215011304/https://law.utexas.edu/transnational/foreign-law-translations/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02479nai a22003377i wotm2003-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || w o    |0    2eng d00aLaw and Politics Book Review. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bAmerican Political Science Association  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Law and Politics Book Review is sponsored by the Law and Courts Section of the American Political Science Association. Reviews are published frequently, and readers are notified by e-mail as new ones are available. The Section has a membership of almost 900 and presently sends the Review to over 1,300 readers in 39 countries. The electronic medium enables us to review almost every book about the legal process and politics, to do longer reviews than are usually published, and to make the reviews available within six months of our receipt of the book. The review presently remains available for an indefinite period on the Review’s World Wide Web home page.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawxBook reviews. 0aPolitical sciencexBook reviews. 0aCourtsxBook reviews. 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261392 aAmerican Political Science Association,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7906625540uhttp://www.lpbr.net413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261009152610/http://www.lpbr.netzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02474nai a22003617i wotm2003-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)5761609600aCenter for Religious Freedom. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bHudson Institute, Inc.  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aCenter is a self-sustaining division of Freedom House, an American human rights group. Its objective is to defend against religious persecution of all groups throughout the world. The website contains current news, country profiles, newsletters, and other relevant information.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aFreedom of religion.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85112662 0aReligious tolerance.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85112746 0aHuman rights 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website2 aHudson Institute,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7903283140uhttps://www.hudson.org/policy-centers/center-religious-freedom#:~:text=When%20US%20policy%20falls%20short,religious%20believers%20persecuted%20under%20Communism413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261010035930/https://www.hudson.org/policy-centers/center-religious-freedom#:~:text=When%20US%20policy%20falls%20short,religious%20believers%20persecuted%20under%20CommunismzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02557nai a22003617i wotm2003-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---04aThe Supreme Court.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aThe History of the Supreme Court 1a[Arlington, Virginia] :bPBS  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2007-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“…this very thorough website was created to complement a major television series on the history of the Supreme Court that will soon appear on PBS. Within each one of the site’s sections, users will find essays and teaching materials on gender equality, social rights, personal liberties, and equal access to schools. The site also includes a very nice interactive timeline of landmark cases handed down since 1792. Finally, the site also includes a searchable encyclopedia of terms and court cases of note.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States. Supreme CourtxHistory. 0aConstitutional historyzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85139984 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 7aEncyclopedias.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260922 aPublic Broadcasting Service (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8613453240uhttps://whyy.pbslearningmedia.org/collection/sup/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261110210455/https://thinktv.pbslearningmedia.org/collection/sup/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02804nai a22003617i wotm2003-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aIndian Trust, Cobell v. Norton. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-12 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aProvided by the Blackfeet Reservation Development Fund, Inc. The site details “a class-action lawsuit filed on June 10, 1996, in U.S. District Court in Washington, D.C. to force the federal government to account for billions of dollars belonging to approximately 500,000 American Indians and their heirs, and held in trust since the late 19th century.” A case overview provides basic background to the litigation, as well as a timeline detailing all major events in the litigation. Court documents, including plaintiff briefs, trial transcripts, court opinions, and letters are all available online in PDF. Media coverage, from the inception of the case to the present, is provided with full text newspaper articles, editorials, press releases, and interviews.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aIndians of North AmericaxLegal status, laws, etc.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85065315 0aIndians of North AmericaxClaims.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85065228 0aIndigenous peoples & tribal law 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 0aTribal / Indigenous nations 6aDigital archive / collection 7aRecords and briefs.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026524403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20140103235152/http://www.indiantrust.comzArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02424nai a22003617i wotm2003-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nbu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aEarly Recognized Treaties with American Indian Nations. 1a[Lincoln, Neb.] :bUniversity of Nebraska  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-12 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aDigitized collection of the nine remaining American Indian treaties created between the years 1722 and 1805, which are not included in Kappler’s Indian affairs: laws and treaties. The collection includes the seven early treaties between a number of American Indian nations and the British, and of two treaties with the United States that were never published in the Statutes at large.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aIndians of North AmericaxTreaties.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85065399 0aIndigenous peoples & tribal law 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aTribal / Indigenous nations 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aTreaties.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110267072 aUniversity of Nebraska--Lincoln.bLibraries,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8002259840uhttp://treatiesportal.unl.edu/earlytreaties/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250725185331/http://treatiesportal.unl.edu/earlytreaties/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03106nai a22004337i wotm2003-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999mou|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)469183518  an-us---00aU.S. Supreme Court Databases.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aSupreme Court Database 1a[St. Louis, Mo.] :bWashington University Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003, 2010).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-12 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis data collection encompasses all aspects of United States Supreme Court decision-making from the 1946 term to the most recent term. Datasets are also available by various terms, and by individual justices for certain terms.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aBased on a database created by Harold J. Spaeth, the website contains over two hundred pieces of information about each case decided by the Court between the 1953 and 2008 terms. Examples include the identity of the court whose decision the Supreme Court reviewed, the parties to the suit, the legal provisions considered in the case, and the votes of the Justices.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aUnited States.bSupreme CourtvCases.10aUnited States.bSupreme Court.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790068481http://isni.org/isni/000000012176610X10aUnited States.bSupreme CourtxHistoryy20th century. 0aJudicial processzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106241 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261812 aWashington University (Saint Louis, Mo.). School of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8107678540uhttp://scdb.wustl.edu413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260913190204/http://scdb.wustl.eduzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02404nai a22003737i wotm2003-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)78099618  an-us---04aThe U.S. Courts of Appeals Database. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bDon Songer Project  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-12 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“The Appeals Court Database Project was designed to create an extensive dataset to facilitate the empirical analysis of the votes of judges and the decisions of the U.S. Courts of Appeals…the database was designed to code a random sample of cases since 1925.”–Home pagecLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAppellate courtszUnited StatesvCases. 0aAppellate courtszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007101194 0aJudicial processzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106241 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402618140uhttp://www.songerproject.org/us-courts-of-appeals-databases.html413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261016124009/http://www.songerproject.org/us-courts-of-appeals-databases.htmlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02220nai a22003737i wotm2003-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)4479172200aNewslink. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bNewslink  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2003).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2006-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aProvides links to both general and special audience newspapers available online, as well as to other news sources such as magazines and radio and television stations. Coverage is worldwide.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aNewspapersxComputer network resourcesvDirectories. 0aElectronic newspapersvDirectories. 0aNews agenciesxComputer network resourcesvDirectories. 0aPressxComputer network resourcesvDirectories. 0aNews radio stationsxComputer network resourcesvDirectories. 0aTelevision stationsxComputer network resourcesvDirectories. 0aGeneral reference (not law-specific) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites)403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260107151540/http://www.newslink.orgzArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02749nai a22004097i wotm2004-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| d o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)43563073  an-us---00aFed in Print :bAn Index to Federal Reserve Economic Research. 1a[San Francisco, Calif.] :bFederal Reserve Bank  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis searchable catalog is hosted on the Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco website, and also contains links to the Latest Working Papers and New Economic Articles.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aFederal Reserve banksvDatabases. 0aBanks and bankingzUnited StatesvDatabases. 0aFinancezUnited StatesvDatabases.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh88002122 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 0aUnited States (federal) 7aIndexes.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026112 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aFederal Reserve Bank of San Francisco,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n5000115140uhttps://fedinprint.org/about413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261013172432/https://fedinprint.org/aboutzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.423Comparable current resource: Fed in Print (FRASER archive of the print index)uhttps://fraser.stlouisfed.org/title/fed-print-9862423Comparable current resource, archived version: Fed in Print (FRASER archive of the print index)uhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260513123118/https://fraser.stlouisfed.org/title/fed-print-9862zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02711nai a22003497i wotm2004-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ilu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aCongressLink. 1a[Pekin, Ill.] :bDirksen Congressional Center  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note, name headings. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aCongressLink is produced by the Dirksen Congressional Center, a non-partisan, not-for-profit organization that seeks to improve public engagement in politics through better understanding of Congress. The website provides information about the U.S. Congress, how it works, its members and leaders, and the public policies it produces. One of its projects is the Civil Rights Documentation Project, which describes the legislative process involved in the struggle to pass the Civil Rights Act of 1964. The project web page provides a detailed, month by month timeline of that development, from January 1963 through the law?s enactment in August 1965. Icons indicate whether a timeline date focuses on the social context or legislative process, and names of key politicians and cites to specific bill numbers are included.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States. Congress.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79006865 0aLegislationzUnited States. 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aEverett McKinley Dirksen Congressional Leadership Research Center,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7802603640uhttps://www.loc.gov/item/2003557479413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260504203517/https://www.loc.gov/item/2003557479zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02511nai a22003497i wotm2004-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)81275016  an-us---04aThe Rutherford Institute Home Page. 1a[Charlottesville, Virginia] :bThe Rutherford Institute  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Rutherford Institute was founded in 1982 by attorney and author John W. Whitehead. As a “civil liberties organization that provides free legal services to people whose constitutional and human rights have been threatened or violated,” the Institute has a mission to both litigate in defense of religious and civil liberties and to educate the public about constitutional rights. The website provides extensive information about Rutherford and its issues of focus. These issues include free speech, religious freedom, church rights, parents rights, zero tolerance, search and seizure, death penalty, and sexual harassment.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCivil rightszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85026377 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aRutherford Institute,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8223694740uhttps://www.rutherford.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261026233316/https://www.rutherford.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03396nai a22003977i wotm2004-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)6241603600aUnited Nations Permanent Forum on Indigenous Issues.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aUN Permanent Forum on Indigenous Issues 1a[New York] :bUN Department of Economic & Social Affairs  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Forum acts as an advisory body to the United Nations Economic and Social Council, and it is charged with providing “expert advice and recommendations” to the Council and to “raise awareness and promote the integration and coordination of activities relating to indigenous issues within the United Nations system.” The website provides a variety of information and materials on the Forum. The history and mandate of the Forum are described in detail. Details of the Forum’s members, secretariat, and monthly calendar are available. Of particular interest to researchers are the articles, speeches, and official documents made available. Speeches include statements and messages delivered by Forum officials. Various background documents and resolutions are included in the official documents section listed by symbol number. The Forum’s session documents are also available.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aPermanent Forum on Indigenous Issues (United Nations)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20030436901http://isni.org/isni/0000000122847040 0aIndigenous peoplesxEconomic conditions.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh95007008 0aIndigenous peoplesxCivil rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2001006129 0aIndigenous peoples & tribal law 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website2 aUnited Nations.bDepartment of Economic and Social Affairs,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790063972 aPermanent Forum on Indigenous Issues (United Nations),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200304369040uhttps://social.desa.un.org/issues/indigenous-peoples/unpfii413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260505171509/https://social.desa.un.org/issues/indigenous-peoples/unpfiizBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02356nai a22003497i wotm2004-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuumau|| w o    |0    2eng d00aNew England Journal of International and Comparative Law. 1a[Boston, Mass.] :bNew England School of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the website, “(t)he articles are scholarly pieces, written by students and legal professionals focusing on provocative current issues and trends in international and comparative law. The publication is intended to serve as a forum for analysis of international legal topics that is both useful and thought provoking.” .cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aInternational lawvPeriodicals. 0aComparative lawvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101406 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aInternational law & organizations 0aForeign & comparative law 0aInternational / multinational 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263522 aNew England School of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n81090554403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20080116001754/http://www.nesl.edu/intljournal/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02347nai a22003977i wotm2004-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| d o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)48526422  an-us---00aCrime & Justice Data Online. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aContinued by a successor resource (linked below).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThis site presents statistics on crime and justice in the United States, including information about crime trends, homicide trends and characteristics, law enforcement management, and administrative statistics. Statistics for state and local agencies are available.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCriminal statisticszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101933 0aHomicidezUnited StatesvStatistics. 0aLaw enforcementzUnited StatesvStatistics. 0aCriminal law & criminal justice 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026181 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260811 aUnited States.bBureau of Justice Statistics,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8003336400tFBI Crime Data Explorer423Successor resource: FBI Crime Data Exploreruhttps://cde.ucr.cjis.gov/02152nai a22003257i wotm2004-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| w o    |0    2mul d  a(OCoLC)5223028700aDirectory of Open Access Journals (DOAJ). 1a[London] :bInfrastructure Services for Open Access C.I.C.  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe DOAJ lists free, full text, quality controlled scientific and scholarly journals, and aims to cover all subjects and languages. As of today (8/1/07), there are 2,795 journals in the directory; 834 of the journals are searchable at article level; 141,333 articles are included; and 53 journals are listed under the Law subject heading. Of the law-related journals, most are either entirely in English or provide some English language articles.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aOpen access publishingvDirectories. 0aElectronic journalsvDirectories. 0aScholarly periodicalsvDirectories. 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 7aDirectories.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402608740uhttps://doaj.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260831162116/https://doaj.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03005nai a22003617i wotm2004-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| d o    i0    2mul d  a(OCoLC)4818138600aOfficial Document System of the United Nations. 1a[New York] :bUnited Nations  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe United Nations Official Documents System (ODS) is the electronic repository for official documents published by the United Nations. It comprises the full text of United Nations parliamentary documents (including resolutions and decisions) issued at United Nations Headquarters in New York and the United Nations Office in Geneva since 1993 as well as at the United Nations Office in Vienna since 1997. The number of duty stations covered by the ODS is expanding as the regional commissions have started to load documents. In addition to parliamentary documentation, United Nations administrative issuances (ST/AI/-, ST/IC/- and ST/SGB/-), considered valid at time of input, are included in the database. UN Resolutions, which includes the official records version of resolutions of the General Assembly, Security Council, Economic and Social Council and Trusteeship Council since 1946. Earlier UN documents (prior to 1993) are being added daily.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited Nations.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98000836 0aInternational agency publications.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh88007406 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational / multinational 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aRecords (Documents).2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261632 aUnited Nations,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7902134540uhttps://documents.un.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261024214849/https://documents.un.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02192nai a22003737i wotm2004-0920