 not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aGovSpot is a government information portal, simplifying the search for government websites, documents, facts and figures, news, public policy information and political organizations.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPolitical sciencevDirectories. 0aElectronic government informationzUnited StatesvDirectories. 0aPublic institutionszUnited StatesvDirectories. 0aUnited StatesxPolitics and governmentvDirectories. 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites)403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20220131154444/http://govspot.com/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02775nai a22003617i wotm2004-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999txu|| d o    s0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)126855087  an-us---00aActual Innocence Awareness Database. 1a[Austin, Texas] :bTarlton Law Library, University of Texas, Austin  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2004).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“The Actual Innocence awareness database provides a listing of United States resources to those interested in the area of wrongful convictions. It encompasses the categories of popular media (such as newspaper articles and segments which aired on television news magazines), journal articles, books, reports, legislation and websites. The materials are classified into what are considered the primary causes of wrongful conviction: forensics/DNA; eyewitness identification; false confessions; jailhouse informants; police and/or prosecutorial misconduct; and ineffective representation. There is also a “general” category for those items which defy further categorization.”–Home page.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aJudicial errorzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008122557 0aFalse imprisonmentzUnited States. 0aCriminal law & criminal justice 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 7aBibliographies.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026048 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402608140uhttps://search.worldcat.org/title/Actual-innocence-awareness-database/oclc/126855087413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250410144137/https://search.worldcat.org/title/Actual-innocence-awareness-database/oclc/126855087zBackup c