multinational 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aTreaties.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026707403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20070710175406/http://lawweb.colorado.edu/eesi/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.423Comparable current resource: IEA Policies and Measures Databaseuhttps://www.iea.org/policies/about423Comparable current resource, archived version: IEA Policies and Measures Databaseuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029050236/https://www.iea.org/policies/aboutzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.423Comparable current resource: International Environmental Agreements (IEA) Databaseuhttps://www.iea.ulaval.ca/en/about/iea-database-project423Comparable current resource, archived version: International Environmental Agreements (IEA) Databaseuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260614185625/https://www.iea.ulaval.ca/en/about/iea-database-projectzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02438nai a22003497i wotm2005-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || w o    f0    2eng d  an-us---04aThe Presidential Timeline of the Twentieth Century. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-03 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Presidential Timeline is a gateway to the digitized collections of the twelve Presidential Libraries of the National Archives, from Herbert Hoover to Bill Clinton. It includes an interactive timeline, educational activities, and also documents, photographs, audio recordings, and video relating to the events of the presidents’ lives.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPresidentszUnited StatesxHistoryx20th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008109605 0aPresidential librarieszUnited States. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20220260791 aUnited States.bNational Archives and Records Administration,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n84176101403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20070909102902/http://www.presidentialtimeline.org:80/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02818nai a22003617i wotm2005-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  an-us---04aThe James Madison Papers. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bLibrary of Congress  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-03 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site consists of approximately 12,000 items housed in the Library of Congress Manuscript Division, captured in some 72,000 digital images, including correspondence, personal notes, drafts of letters and legislation, an autobiography, legal and financial documents, and miscellaneous manuscripts. Highlights include a copy of Thomas Jefferson’s notes from the Continental Congress of 1776, including Jefferson’s copy of the Declaration of Independence as amended by Congress. Among Madison’s correspondents were Jefferson, Dolly Madison, James Monroe, Alexander Hamilton, George Washington, and Noah Webster.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPresidentszUnited StatesvArchives.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85106466 0aConstitutional historyzUnited StatesvSources.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101624 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20220260792 aLibrary of Congress,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780890352 aLibrary of Congress.bManuscript Division,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7808064240uhttps://www.loc.gov/collections/james-madison-papers/about-this-collection/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260820220638/https://www.loc.gov/collections/james-madison-papers/about-this-collection/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03126nai a22003857i wotm2005-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)51177502  an-us---04aThe Martin Luther King, Jr. Papers Project at Stanford University. 1a[Stanford, California] :bStanford University  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site was chosen as one of the “Best Free Reference Web Sites of 2000” by RUSA Quarterly. According to the website’s Overview, “[t]he King Papers Project is a major research effort to assemble and disseminate historical information concerning Martin Luther King, Jr. and the social movements in which he participated.” In addition to an extensive King Biography, Encyclopedia, and collection of Audio recordings, the website includes the most complete inventory available of King’s major sermons, speeches, public statements, published writings, manuscripts, and substantial notes and outlines. Each of the 1,750 catalog records in the inventory contains information that enables scholars to identify the documents and determine the archival location of the original.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAfrican AmericansxCivil rightsxHistoryx20th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100199 0aCivil rights movementszUnited StatesxHistoryx20th century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100355 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20220260792 aMartin Luther King, Jr. Papers Project,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n896676752 aStanford University,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7905463640uhttps://kinginstitute.stanford.edu/king-papers/about-papers-project413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261020192532/https://kinginstitute.stanford.edu/king-papers/about-papers-projectzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02972nai a22003857i wotm2005-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999miu|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)76699337  an-us---04aThe Civil Rights Litigation Clearinghouse. 1a[Ann Arbor, Michigan] :bUniversity of Michigan Law School  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the website, “The Civil Rights Litigation Clearinghouse is a collection of documents and information about civil rights cases in selected case categories across the United States. Currently, the categories include: Child Welfare, Criminal Justice (Other), Disability Rights-Pub. Accom., Education, Election/Voting Rights, Equal Employment, Fair Housing/Lending/Insurance, Immigration, Jail Conditions, Juvenile Institution, Mental Health Facility, Mental Retardation Facility, Nursing Home Conditions, Policing, Prison Conditions, Public Benefits, Public Defenders, Public Housing, School Desegregation, Speech and Religious Freedom. The site is dedicated to injunctive rather than damages litigation — that is, to cases seeking policy or operational change, not cases seeking money.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCivil rightszUnited StatesvCases.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100366 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aRecords and briefs.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110265242 aUniversity of Michigan.bLaw School,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8211698140uhttps://clearinghouse.net413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260917041106/https://clearinghouse.netzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03404nai a22004217i wotm2005-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)59284765  an-us---04aThe Pew Forum on Religion & Public Life. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aLaunched in 2001, this site seeks to promote a deeper understanding of issues at the intersection of religion and public affairs. The Forum focuses on four key areas of research: Religion and Politics (where the focus is on the influence of religion and religious organizations on political behavior, including voting and campaigns); Religion and the Law (where the Forum analyzes church-state controversies such as Supreme Court battles over the Ten Commandments, the Pledge of Allegiance and school vouchers); Religion and Domestic Policy (where the Forum examines a wide range of policy debates from abortion and gay marriage to stem cell research and faith-based initiatives); and Religion and World Affairs (where it explores the integral role religion plays in world affairs, with a particular focus on religions impact on U.S. foreign policy).cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aReligion and lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010110637 0aChurch and statezUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100716 0aReligion and politicszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008110386 0aReligion and statezUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008110661 0aChristianity and politicszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008117672 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aPew Forum on Religion & Public Life,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200207833900tPew Research Center: Religion423Successor resource: Pew Research Center: Religionuhttps://www.pewresearch.org/topic/religion/423Successor resource, archived version: Pew Research Center: Religionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261108145607/https://www.pewresearch.org/topic/religion/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02413nai a22003497i wotm2005-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aNACA - National Association of Consumer Advocates.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:anaca.net 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bNational Association of Consumer Advocates  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe homepage of the National Association of Consumer Advocates, this site provides general information about issues affecting consumers such as auto fraud, binding mandatory arbitration, credit reporting problems, debt collection abuse, identity theft, lemon law, military consumer rights, predatory lending practices, and student loans. The site also has an extensive collection of amicus briefs.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aConsumer protectionxLaw and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101115 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website 7aRecords and briefs.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110265242 aNational Association of Consumer Advocates,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr9703465840uhttps://www.consumeradvocates.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261008074921/https://www.consumeradvocates.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02396nai a22003497i wotm2005-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuunyu|| d o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aAltLaw. 1a[New York] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site provides the first free, full-text searchable database of Supreme Court and Federal Appellate case reports. It is a resource for attorneys, legal scholars, and the general public. AltLaw is a joint project of Columbia Law School’s Program on Law and Technology, and the Silicon Flatirons Program at the University of Colorado Law School, and is a work in progress.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLaw reports, digests, etc.zUnited StatesvDatabases. 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110261722 aColumbia University.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n82167055423Comparable current resource: CourtListeneruhttps://www.courtlistener.com/423Comparable current resource, archived version: CourtListeneruhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261109211855/https://www.courtlistener.com/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02567nai a22003497i wotm2005-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| w o    f0    2eng d00aResearch-Based Web Design and Usability Guidelines.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aResearch-based Web Design & Usability Guidelines 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bU.S. Department of Health & Human Services  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThese guidelines were originally designed to help National Cancer Institute staff improve the presentation of cancer-related information to cancer researchers and the public, though they are applicable to anyone who designs and manages information web sites.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aWeb sitesxDesign.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98000035 0aWeb site development.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98004795 0aUser-centered system design.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006002024 0aGeneral reference (not law-specific) 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261091 aUnited States.bDepartment of Health and Human Services,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n80102594403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260301234044/https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/research-based-web-design-and-usability-guidelines_book.pdfzArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.03048nai a22003857i wotm2005-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cou|| d o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aNational Indian Law Library.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aNational Indian Law Library (Nill) 1a[Boulder, Colo.] :bNative American Rights Fund  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to NILL’s homepage, “…NILL is a public law library devoted to federal Indian and tribal law. Our mission is to develop and make accessible a unique and valuable collection of Indian law resources and other information relating to Native Americans. NILL places special emphasis on fulfilling the information needs of Indian law advocates and others working on behalf of Native Americans.” The library serves all members of the general public including individuals and organizations working on behalf of Native Americans. In addition to the library catalog and lists of resources by topic, the site features the Tribal Law Gateway which is a database for finding constitutions and codes of federally recognized tribes, and an online collection of digitized codes and constitutions. The site also provides a current awareness service called Indian Law Bulletins.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aIndians of North AmericaxLegal status, laws, etc.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85065315 0aLaw librarieszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009129189 0aIndigenous peoples & tribal law 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 0aTribal / Indigenous nations 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aNative American Rights Fund,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n5006612740uhttps://www.narf.org/nill/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261021022355/https://www.narf.org/nill/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02902nai a22003857i wotm2005-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aTobacco Control Archives. 1a[San Francisco] :bUniversity of California San Francisco  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Tobacco Control Archives (TCA) is a print and digital collection of papers, documents, and electronic resources related to tobacco control issues maintained by Galen, the digital library of the University of California at San Francisco. The primary digital collection is the ?Legacy Tobacco Documents Library? which consists of over ?7 million documents concerning scientific research, manufacturing, marketing, advertising, and sales of cigarettes.? Also available through TCA are the complaints and other tobacco litigation documents filed by the Attorneys General of 44 states, government reports on tobacco industry, and some e-books. Finally, detailed finding aids for the paper collections are available online.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aTobaccoxLaw and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010116586 0aTobacco industryzUnited StatesvArchives. 0aAntismoking movementzUnited States. 0aHealth, disability & social welfare 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aRecords (Documents).2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261632 aUniversity of California, San Francisco.bLibrary,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9102354640uhttps://www.library.ucsf.edu/archives/tobacco/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260715162341/https://www.library.ucsf.edu/archives/tobacco/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02313nai a22003617i wotm2005-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)166273314  an-us---00aACS ResearchLink. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aA project of the American Constitution Society for Law and Policy, this site collects legal research topics submitted by practitioners for law students to explore in faculty-supervised writing projects for academic credit.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075193 0aLegal researchzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106837 0aLawxStudy and teachingzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106829 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20150801151757/http://researchlink.acslaw.org/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.03769nai a22003977i wotm2005-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)54097040  an-us---00aBoard of Governors of the Federal Reserve System. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bFederal Reserve System  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2005).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis is the official website of the Federal Reserve, the central bank of the United States. The site presents detailed information about the Federal Reserve system, its board of governors, Federal Reserve banks, and monetary policy. The site also provides access to information on payment systems, economic research and data, consumer information, reporting forms, and online publications. This site was named one of the “Best Free Reference Web Sites 2004;” and received this review in the RUSA Quarterly: “Maintained by the governing body of the Federal Reserve, this site provides an excellent gateway for the Federal Reserve System as a whole. Both banking professionals and those with a general interest in the economy will find useful features on this site. A search engine, as well as topical links, lead the user to rich descriptive and full-text material that includes press releases, statistical data, speeches, publications, and consumer information. In addition to descriptions of the twelve Federal Reserve district banks, there is an electronic map which links to the district homepages, which provide valuable information about different regional economies. This site is an excellent starting point for anyone interested in banking at the federal level or the economy as a whole.”–Reviewed March 5, 2004 “Best Free Reference Web Sites 2004,” RUSA Quarterly, Fall 2004. Comp. by the MARS Best Free Websites Committee, RUSA, ALA.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aBoard of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (U.S.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780912831http://isni.org/isni/0000000404787576 0aFederal Reserve banks.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85047618 0aMonetary policyzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008107909 0aCreditzUnited States. 0aFinancezUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh90001493 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website2 aBoard of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7809128340uhttps://www.federalreserve.gov413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261031180821/https://www.federalreserve.govzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02118nai a22003617i wotm2006-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)637792412  an-us---00aCato Journal. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bCato Institute  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-05 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Cato journal is a public policy journal that is written and edited to be accessible to lay readers.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month