s 0aInternational criminal law & transitional justice 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aInternational / multinational 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402613940uhttps://www.boomportaal.nl/tijdschrift/HJJ413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250218034615/https://www.elevenjournals.com/tijdschrift/hjj/2009/3zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02560nai a22003377i wotm2006-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuucau|| d o    s0    2eng d00aELS Bibliography. 1a[Los Angeles] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-05 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe ELS bibliography is a database hosted by the UCLA School of Law that contains empirical legal research material published after July 2005. The database includes law reviews from top law schools in the country, major specialty journals, legal journals not published by law schools, and journals in other areas: economics, political science, sociology, anthropology and psychology. Entries include the following bibliographic data: author and affiliation, subject categories, and data in Blue Book format. The articles are searchable by author, title, subject and year.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegal researchzUnited StatesvBibliography. 0aSociological jurisprudencevBibliography. 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aLegal research & reference tools 7aBibliographies.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026048 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aUniversity of California, Los Angeles.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79119351403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20160109060031/http://apps.law.ucla.edu/els/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02342nai a22003737i wotm2006-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999txu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)221975254  an-us---00aLawProse, Inc. Interviews of United States Supreme Court Justices. 1a[Dallas, Texas] :bLawProse, Inc.  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-05 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site presents interviews conducted by Bryan Garner in 2006 and 2007 with 8 of the 9 U.S. Supreme Court Justices. In these interviews, the justices talk about issues such as writing legal briefs and appearing before the court.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegal composition.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075735 0aTrial practicezUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008112924 0aJudgeszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh88002178 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection40uhttps://www.lawprose.org/bryan-garner/videos/supreme-court-interviews/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260608090443/https://www.lawprose.org/bryan-garner/videos/supreme-court-interviews/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02783nai a22003497i wotm2006-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuumau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)45356714  an-us---00aEnvironmental Law Net. 1a[Massachusetts] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aCreated as a client service tool in 1998 by environmental and energy lawyer David Blackmar, Environmental Law Net is a leading resource for environmental law research and news. This site is currently under reconstruction, but currently visitors may access information via the two main content divisions: legal information libraries and community resources. There are six legal information libraries which are broken into document libraries and task-specific libraries. The document libraries cover laws and regulations, court and agency decisions, and other agency documents. The task-specific libraries cover compliance, enforcement and litigation, and real estate and corporate transactions. The community resources area provides a daily newsfeed, reference tools, a moderated interview and seminar forum, editorial articles, and other useful features.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aEnvironmental lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009103157 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 7aLaw materials.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026351403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20160112062641/http://www.environmentallawnet.com/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02413nai a22003857i wotm2006-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)45358020  an-us---00aEnvironmental Council of the States. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bECOS  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aBased in Washington, D.C., Environmental Council of the States (ECOS) is a nonprofit association of state and territorial environmental commissioners. The website highlights the work of ECOS, including the states involved, projects, research, and the policies of ECOS.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aEnvironmental Council of the States (U.S.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no97069076 0aEnvironmental policyzUnited StatesxStates. 0aEnvironmental lawzUnited StatesxStates.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009103278 0aEnvironmental protectionzUnited StatesxStates. 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aOrganization website2 aEnvironmental Council of the States (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9706907640uhttps://www.ecos.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261103014010/https://www.ecos.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02563nai a22003737i wotm2006-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999be || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)71804567  ae------00aEU Environmental Policy Handbook :bA Critical Analysis of EU Environmental Legislation : Making It Accessible to Environmentalists and Decision Makers. 1a[Brussels] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis 2005 book was edited by Stefan Scheuer. It describes the history and current status of EU environmental law, and also looks to the future by analysing the strengths and weaknesses of the actions taken so far.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aEnvironmental lawzEuropean Union countriesvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 0aEnvironmental policyzEuropean Union countriesvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aEuropean Union 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261092 aEuropean Environmental Bureau,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8316563740uhttps://jak.ppke.hu/storage/tinymce/uploads/old/uploads/articles/719134/file/EU%20Policy%20Handbook%20.pdf413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261110210611/https://jak.ppke.hu/storage/tinymce/uploads/old/uploads/articles/719134/file/EU%20Policy%20Handbook%20.pdfzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02979nai a22003257i wotm2006-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d04aThe Journal of Philosophy, Science & Law. 1a[Charlottesville, Virginia] :bPhilosophy Documentation Center  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThis journal is sponsored by the University of Miami’s Ethics Program and the Georgia Institute of Technology’s School of Public Policy. According to the journal’s website, it “is an interdisciplinary forum dedicated to examining issues in the intersection of applied philosophy, science, and the law. The Journal seeks to stimulate research and publish articles in the following areas: Philosophical issues associated with science policy and the growth of technology; Philosophy, the legal system, and scientific evidence; The influence of legal and ethical guidelines on scientific research; and Educational issues relating to how legal and ethical guidelines are taught within scientific fields.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawxPhilosophyvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106740 0aScience and lawvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010112148 0aEvidence, ExpertvPeriodicals. 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aIntellectual property, technology & privacy 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263522 aPhilosophy Documentation Center,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200411068240uhttps://www.pdcnet.org/jpsl/The-Journal-of-Philosophy,-Science-&-Law#:~:text=The%20Journal%20of%20Philosophy%2C%20Science%20%26%20Law%20is%20an%20interdisciplinary%20forum,legal%20system%2C%20and%20scientific%20evidence413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261017151845/https://www.pdcnet.org/jpsl/The-Journal-of-Philosophy,-Science-&-Law#:~:text=The%20Journal%20of%20Philosophy%2C%20Science%20%26%20Law%20is%20an%20interdisciplinary%20forum,legal%20system%2C%20and%20scientific%20evidencezBackup copy in 