nline resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2006).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-04 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe final 2 titles for March 2008 are the Stanford Agora: an Online Journal of Legal Perspectives and its predecessor, the Stanford journal of legal studies. According to the Agora’s website, it “is an exclusively online journal that seeks to enrich legal discourse by creating a forum for the discussion of vital legal issues by lawyers and non-lawyers alike. “Agora” is the ancient Greek word for “marketplace”. The Greek Agora served as a forum for philosophical discussion and debate. Today the desire for intense intellectual interaction has not waned, but the forum for discussion has moved: today’s agora is the Internet. Capitalizing on this revolutionary platform, Stanford Agora supplements traditional written content with multimedia texts and interactive elements.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzCaliforniavPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106729 0aLaw reviewszCalifornia.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106728 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263522 aStanford University,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/