60792 aUniversity of California, Santa Barbara,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8012630340uhttps://www.presidency.ucsb.edu413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261103182533/https://www.presidency.ucsb.eduzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.01976nai a22003257i wotm2007-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999gw || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)4845194500aGlobal Corruption Report. 1a[Berlin] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThese annual reports each have a thematic title, and are issued in English, French, German, and Spanish editions.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPolitical corruptionvPeriodicals. 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aInternational / multinational 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261392 aTransparency International,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9701064540uhttps://www.transparency.org/en/publications/global-corruption-report-2009413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261006071458/https://www.transparency.org/en/publications/global-corruption-report-2009zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02619nai a22003257i wotm2007-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| w o    |0    2eng d00aGCS PolicyArchive.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aCgs – Policyarchive 1a[Los Angeles] :bCenter for Governmental Studies  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site is a project of the Center for Governmental Studies and Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis University Library. According to the site’s Press Room page, “PolicyArchive is an innovative, new digital archive of global, non-partisan public policy research. It houses summaries and full texts of public policy research from various think tanks, universities, government agencies, and foundations. It allows research users, policy makers, the media, and the public to quickly access the depth and breadth of research in numerous subject matters. Ultimately, PolicyArchive will indefinitely preserve the life of public policy research, substantially increase its impact, and provide society at large with long-term access to the benefits of that important research.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPolicy sciencesvDatabases. 0aPolitical planningvDatabases. 0aGovernment information & administrative law 6aDigital archive / collection2 aCenter for Governmental Studies (Los Angeles, Calif.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9908180040uhttps://www.policyarchive.org/collections/cgs/index413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20220306041930/https://www.policyarchive.org/collections/cgs/indexzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02433nai a22003497i wotm2007-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999pau|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aFactCheck.org :bAnnenberg Political Fact Check. 1a[Philadelphia] :bAnnenberg Public Policy Center  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site is a nonpartisan, nonprofit, “consumer advocate” for voters that aims to reduce the level of deception and confusion in U.S. politics. The site monitors the factual accuracy of what is said by major U.S. political players in the form of TV ads, debates, speeches, interviews, and news releases. Its goal is to apply the best practices of both journalism and scholarship, and to increase public knowledge and understanding.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPolitical campaignszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008109540 0aAdvertising, PoliticalzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100692 0aTruthfulness and falsehoodxPolitical aspectszUnited States. 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aAnnenberg Public Policy Center,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr9503120740uhttps://www.factcheck.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20070104161229/https://www.factcheck.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03971nai a22004817i wotm2007-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)51722927  an-us---00aOpenSecrets.org :bThe Website of the Center for Responsive Politics. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bCenter for Responsive Politics  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  a“The Center for Responsive Politics describes itself as ‘a non-partisan, non-profit research group based in Washington, D.C. that tracks money in politics, and its effect on elections and public policy.’ Opensecrets.org, the Center’s Web site, provides information from the Federal Election Commission about campaign contributions to Congress, to the political parties and the presidential campaigns. The site may be navigated by tabs at the top of the web page, by search engines within the site, or by links to current issues. Everything is documented with citations and methodology. The mission statement, contact information, and funding sources are clearly noted. Opensecrets.org is a goldmine of data on contributions in politics, helpful both for students writing papers and for avid followers of politics”–“Best Free Reference Web Sites 2002,” RUSA Quarterly, Fall 2002; reviewed Feb. 19, 2002cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aCenter for Responsive Politics (Washington, D.C.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n879438221http://isni.org/isni/000000012167074910aUnited States.bCongressxElections.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140773 0aCampaign fundszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100035 0aPolitical action committeeszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008109539 0aPolitical participationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008109399 0aLobbyingzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106892 0aPoliticianszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85104464 0aPolicy sciences.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85104264 0aCampaign fundsxResearch. 0aElections.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85041557 0aWashington (D.C.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79018774 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261812 aCenter for Responsive Politics (Washington, D.C.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8794382240uhttps://www.opensecrets.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261017182135/https://www.opensecrets.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02444nai a22003737i wotm2007-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)228161438  an-us---00aJust Regulation Tracker.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aJustia Regulation Tracker 1a[Mountain View, Calif.] :bJustia  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site provides free access to Federal rules, proposed rules, notices, administrative orders, executive orders, and proclamations. Users may search by department or agency, include keywords, and limit by document type or date; or browse by agency or date. Coverage begins January 1, 2005cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAdministrative lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100599 0aDelegated legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008102143 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aAdministrative regulations.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102603040uhttps://regulations.justia.com/regulations/fedreg/agencies413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250717204746/https://regulations.justia.com/regulations/fedreg/agencieszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02723nai a22004097i wotm2007-06