nb200701624600tlegislation.gov.uk423Successor resource: legislation.gov.ukuhttps://www.legislation.gov.uk423Successor resource, archived version: legislation.gov.ukuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261108185908/https://www.legislation.gov.ukzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03476nai a22004937i wotm2007-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999onc|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)528374554  an-cn---00aCanLII :bCanadian Legal Information Institute.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aCanLII 1a[Ottawa] :bCanadian Legal information Institute  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007, 2024).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aFeatured between 2024-12 and 2025-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aTitle, publication and subject data from the University of Hawaiʻi Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site provides access to primary sources of Canadian Law accessible for free on the Internet. The site includes legislative and judicial texts, as well as legal commentaries, from federal, provincial, and territorial jurisdictions, and the information is available in both French and English.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aThe Canadian Legal Information Institute (CanLII) is a non-profit organization established in 2001 by the Federation of Law Societies of Canada. Its French title is Institut canadien d’information juridique. CanLII is supported by 14 member law societies and aims to provide efficient access to a comprehensive collection of current judicial decisions and legislative documents. It serves the legal profession by supporting lawyers in their duties and offers the public access to laws and legal cases from all Canadian jurisdictions.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzCanadavDatabases. 0aLaw reports, digests, etc.zCanadavDatabases. 0aLegal researchzCanadavDatabases. 7aLegal research.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00995522 7aLaw reports, digests, etc.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00994106 7aLaw.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00993678 0aForeign & comparative law 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aCanada 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110261722 aCanadian Legal Information Institute,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no202201990940uhttps://www.canlii.org/en/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250316183448/https://www.canlii.org/en/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03483nai a22004577i wotm2007-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuusl || w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)226301727  af-sl---04aThe Special Court for Sierra Leone. 1a[Freetown] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the homepage, “The Special Court for Sierra Leone was set up jointly by the Government of Sierra Leone and the United Nations. It is mandated to try those who bear the greatest responsibility for serious violations of international humanitarian law and Sierra Leonean law committed in the territory of Sierra Leone since 30 November 1996.” The website provides information about the Court, information related to its cases, basic documents of the Court, and practice directions and directives of the Court.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aSpecial Court for Sierra Leone.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr20020390981http://isni.org/isni/0000000106887421 0aInternational criminal courts.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh94003151 0aInternational criminal law & transitional justice 0aInternational / multinational 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aSierra Leone 6aOrganization website 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110261722 aSpecial Court for Sierra Leone,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr200203909800tRSCSL Document and Video Archive403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20110222042707/http://www.sc-sl.org/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.423Successor resource: RSCSL Document and Video Archiveuhttps://docs.rscsl.org423Successor resource, archived version: RSCSL Document and Video Archiveuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261110210645/https://docs.rscsl.org/documentszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.423Successor resource: Residual Special Court for Sierra Leoneuhttps://rscsl.org/423Successor resource, archived version: Residual Special Court for Sierra Leoneuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261017044518/https://rscsl.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03154nai a22003857i wotm2007-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999gw || w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)5854147904aThe International Tribunal for the Law of the Sea. 1a[Hamburg, Germany] :bInternational Tribunal for the Law of the Seas  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea entered into force on 16 November 1994. A subsequent Agreement relating to the implementation of Part XI of the Convention entered into force on 28 July 1996. The International Tribunal for the Law of the Sea is an independent judicial body established by the Convention to adjudicate disputes arising out of the interpretation and application of the Convention. The Tribunal is composed of 21 elected independent members. This site provides general information, proceedings and judgments, documents and publications, news, and question and answer sections in both English and French.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aInternational Tribunal for the Law of the Sea.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n879230111http://isni.org/isni/0000000119414519 0aLaw of the sea.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh97008889 0aInternational courts.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85067388 0aInternational law & organizations 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website 7aCourt decisions and opinions.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110261722 aInternational Tribunal for the Law of the Sea,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8792301140uhttps://www.itlos.org/en/main/the-tribunal/the-tribunal/#:~:text=The%20International%20Tribunal%20for%20the,and%20application%20of%20the%20Convention413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261103183136/https://www.itlos.org/en/main/the-tribunal/the-tribunal/#:~:text=The%20International%20Tribunal%20for%20the,and%20application%20of%20the%20ConventionzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02864nai a22004097i wotm2007-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999jm || w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)4428491900aInternational Seabed Authority. 1a[Kingston, Jamaica] :bInternational Seabed Authority  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2007).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site contains information on the administrative bodies of the International Seabed Authority, including the Assembly, Council, Legal and Technical Commission, Finance Committee and the Secretariat. This site also includes a list of documents issued by the Authority at each of its sessions, and the full text of selected documents, and the information is available in English, French, or Spanish.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aInternational Seabed Authority.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n791173731http://isni.org/isni/000000012217123900aUnited Nations Convention on the Law of the Sead(1982 December 10)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n83149072 0aLaw of the sea.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh97008889 0aOcean bottomxLaw and legislation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85093881 0aMarine mineral resourcesxLaw and legislation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85081219 0aOcean miningxLaw and legislation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85093897 0aInternational law & organizations 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website2 aInternational Seabed Authority,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7911737340uhttps://isa.org.jm/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261021193504/https://isa.org.jm/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02242nai a22003497i wotm2007-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)47862185  an-us---00aFuelEconomy.gov. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bOffice of Energy Efficiency and Renewable Energy  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-S