05-03 and 2008-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site provides currency conversion information and other services for travelers and businesses.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aOANDA Corporation. 0aCurrency convertibility.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85034876 0aForeign exchange.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85050496 0aGeneral reference (not law-specific) 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402608140uhttps://www.oanda.com/currency-converter/en/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261102084322/https://www.oanda.com/currency-converter/en/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02521nai a22003737i wotm2008-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)49284685  an-us---00aU.S. Commission on Civil Rights. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bU.S. Commission on Civil Rights  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site features the work of the U.S. Commission on Civil Rights (USCCR). Based in Washington, D.C., the USCCR is an independent, bipartisan, fact-finding agency of the Executive Branch that examines and endeavors to resolve discrimination issues related to race, ethnicity, religion and, more recently, sexual orientation.. This site includes the full-text of commission reports, some state advisory commission reports, and other publications.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States Commission on Civil Rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780957781http://isni.org/isni/0000000121941369 0aCivil rightszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85026377 0aDiscriminationzUnited StatesxPrevention. 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website2 aUnited States Commission on Civil Rights,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7809577840uhttps://www.usccr.gov413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261026132051/https://www.usccr.govzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02280nai a22003497i wotm2008-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999mdu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aHistorical Publications of the U.S. Commission on Civil Rights.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aHistorical Publications of the United States Commission on Civil Rights 1a[Baltimore, Md.] :bThurgood Marshall Law Library  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis project is a partnership of the United States Government Printing Office, the United States Commission on Civil Rights and the Thurgood Marshall Law Library. The documents on this site are searchable by title, date, subject, and SUDOC number.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States Commission on Civil Rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n78095778 0aCivil rightszUnited StatesxHistoryvSources.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009120231 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection40uhttps://www2.law.umaryland.edu/marshall/usccr/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260304124454/https://www2.law.umaryland.edu/marshall/usccr/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03125nai a22003857i wotm2008-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)4424637000aCRIN :bChild Rights International Network.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aCRIN: Child Rights Information Network 1a[London] :bCRIN  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aCRIN: Child Rights Information Network is a global network coordinating and promoting information and action on child rights. Almost 2,000 member organisations and tens of thousands more activists from across the world rely on CRIN for research and information. CRIN presses for rights, not charity, for children and is guided by a passion for putting children’s rights at the top of the global agenda by addressing root causes and promoting systematic change. Its guiding framework is the UN Convention on the Rights of the Child (CRC). CRIN’s activities are based on the belief that information is a powerful tool for realising children’s rights. CRIN distributes news, events and reports, lobbies, enables advocacy and promotes knowledge sharing and coordination. CRIN participates in international child rights coalitions and advocacy groups, supports campaigns and makes the UN and regional mechanisms more accessible to those lobbying for social change. “–About CRINcLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aChild Rights Information Network.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20091100251http://isni.org/isni/0000000096714403 0aChildren's rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85023773 0aChild welfare.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85023396 0aHuman rights 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website2 aChild Rights Information Network,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200911002540uhttps://home.crin.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261031182522/https://home.crin.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02667nai a22003977i wotm2008-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)52255699  an-us---00aChildStats.gov. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bFederal Interagency Forum on Child & Family Statistics  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aChildStats.gov: the official Web site of the Federal Interagency Forum on Child and Family Statistics offers easy access to federal and state statistics and reports on children and their families, including: population and family characteristics, economic security, health, behavior and social environment, and education. Childstats.gov is a project of the Federal Interagency Forum on Child and Family Statistics.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aChildrenzUnited StatesvStatistics. 0aChildrenzUnited StatesxSocial conditions.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100386 0aFamilieszUnited StatesvStatistics.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008120206 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aHealth, disability & social welfare 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261812 aFederal Interagency Forum on Child and Family Statistics (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9704838340uhttps://www.childstats.gov413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261019160241/https://www.childstats.govzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.01608nai a22003017i 4500001001200000005001700012006001900029007001500048008004100063245002200104264007200126300002200198336002600220337002600246338003600272500008800308500008100396500007000477500018000547520012600727588012000853650004700973650004501020653004101065653004001106653004501146856011501191wotm2008-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || w o    |0    2eng d00aChildwelfare.com. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aChildwelfare.com is an index to Internet resources on child abuse and child welfare.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aChild welfarexComputer network resources. 0aChild abusexComputer network resources. 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aHealth, disability & social welfare 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites)423Comparable current resource: Child Welfare Information Gateway - Find Resourcesuhttps://www.childwelfare.gov/02643nai a22003977i wotm2008-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)60493066  an-us---00aChildren's Defense Fund.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aChildren’s Defense Fund (CDF) 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bChildren's Defense Fund  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Children’s Defense Fund (CDF) is a nonprofit organization providing a voice for children in America, particularly minority, poor, and disabled children. The CDF’s goal is to educate the nation about children’s needs. The website includes news items, reports, and information on current issues related to children, as well as information on CDF publications, conferences, and products.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aChildren's Defense Fund (U.S.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n800833011http://isni.org/isni/0000000121937394 0aChildrenzUnited StatesxSocial conditions.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100386 0aChildrenxHealth and hygienezUnited States. 0aChildren of minoritieszUnited StatesxSocial conditions. 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aChildren's Defense Fund (U.S.),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8008330140uhttps://www.childrensdefense.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261030001111/https://www.childrensdefense.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02529nai a22003377i wotm2008-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ohu|| w o    s0    2eng d  an-us---00aElection Law @ Moritz :bInformation and Insight on the Laws Governing Federal, State and Local Elections. 1a[Columbus, Ohio] :bOhio State Moritz College of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the site’s “About Us” page, “Election Law @ Moritz is a web publication that covers developments in the law of election administration– laws dealing with voter registration, voter ID, early and absentee voting, provisional balloting, poll workers and polling place procedures, recounts and election contests, and other related issues. Our primary target audience includes lawyers and legal scholars who focus on these issues, as well as journalists in the elections field.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aElection lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2006000055 0aElectionszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85041561 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 7aBlogs.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402605140uhttps://moritzlaw.osu.edu/faculty-and-research/election-law-ohio-state413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261014025959/https://moritzlaw.osu.edu/faculty-and-research/election-law-ohio-statezBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03186nai a22003977i wotm2008-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuucau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)48914985  an-us---00aLegacy Tobacco Documents Library. 1a[San Francisco, California] :bUniversity of California, San Francisco, Library  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2008-10 and 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note, name headings. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aIn honor of the Great American Smokeout on November 20, this month’s other featured site is Legacy tobacco documents library. This site offers searching, viewing, and downloading of over 8 million documents which relate to scientific research, manufacturing, marketing, litigation and legislation, and advertising and sales of cigarettes, among other topics. These documents generally date from the 1950’s to recent years. The Legacy tobacco documents library is part of the Tobacco control archives, which was a previous Website of the Month selection.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aTobacco industryxLaw and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010116577 0aProducts liabilityxTobaccozUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010108575 0aTobaccoxHealth aspects. 0aHealth, disability & social welfare 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 6aDigital archive / collection2 aUniversity of California, San Francisco. Library,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9102354600tTruth Tobacco Industry Documents (UCSF Industry Documents Library)403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20150106131423/http://legacy.library.ucsf.edu/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.423Successor resource: Truth Tobacco Industry Documents (UCSF Industry Documents Library)uhttps://www.industrydocuments.ucsf.edu/tobacco/423Successor resource, archived version: Truth Tobacco Industry Documents (UCSF Industry Documents Library)uhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261028225435/https://www.industrydocuments.ucsf.edu/tobacco/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02637nai a22003737i wotm2008-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999mdu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aLandmark Supreme Court Cases. 1a[Silver Spring, Md.] :bStreet Law/The Supreme Court Historical Society  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured 2008-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site is a collaboration between Street Law and The Supreme Court Historical Society, and was developed to provide teachers with a full range of resources and activities to support the teaching of landmark Supreme Court cases. While these activities are online, many of them can be adapted for use in a one-computer classroom or a classroom with no computer. The general teaching strategies include moot court, political cartoon analysis, continuum exercises, and Web site evaluation.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited States. Supreme Court.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79006848 0aConstitutional lawzUnited StatesvCases.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85139989 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 0aUnited States (federal) 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261092 aStreet Law, Inc,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n980995792 aSupreme Court Historical Society,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8102589640uhttps://landmarkcases.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260115005000/https://landmarkcases.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02817nai a22003617i wotm2008-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)174120275  an-us---04aThe Complete Lawyer :bHow Lawyers Succeed. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aAccording to the home page, this website is devoted to “[t]ools and insights on the professional development, and quality of life, and career issues that impact every lawyer’s success and satisfaction.” On September 25, 2007 the home page explained that “The Complete Lawyer is sponsored by bar associations across the country. It is sent out every sixty days to thousands of lawyers via email and is posted continuously on the web … [It] focuses solely on the personal and professional development of lawyers.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawyerszUnited StatesvPeriodicals.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009129389 0aPractice of lawzUnited StatesvPeriodicals.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2010107991 0aBar associationszUnited StatesvPeriodicals.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009116802 0aLawvPeriodicals.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075138 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 7aPeriodicals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026139423Comparable current resource: ABA Career Center: Personal Development / Wellbeinguhttps://www.americanbar.org/careercenter/wellbeing/423Comparable current resource, archived version: ABA Career Center: Personal Development / Wellbeinguhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250806032117/https://www.americanbar.org/careercenter/wellbeing/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03213nai a22003857i wotm2008-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999lau|| w o    s0    2eng d  an-us-la02aA Digest of Civil Laws Now in Force in the Territory of Orleans.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aA Digest of Civil Laws Now in Force in the Territory of Orleans : With Alterations and Amendments Adapted to Its Present System of Government 1a[Baton Rouge, Louisiana] :bCenter of Civil Law Studies  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site is a joint project of the Center of Civil Law Studies (CCLS), Information Technology and the Law Library of the Paul M. Hebert Law Center, in partnership with the Center for French and Francophone Studies, and the Department of French Studies at Louisiana State University. According to the website, “The Digest of the Civil Laws now in Force in the Territory of Orleans was enacted on March 31, 1808. It is now made accessible online, on occasion of the Bicentennial of what is often described as the first Louisiana civil code. The original French and the English translation can be viewed separately or together on the same screen. The typing of both versions was extracted from the first edition of 1808, printed by Bradford & Anderson, in the city of New Orleans. With the exception of obvious typos, the Digest Online strictly follows the original wording and orthography.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCivil lawzLouisiana.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009120032 0aLawzLouisianaxHistoryvSources. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 5aLouisiana 6aDigital archive / collection 7aStatutes and codes.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110266112 aLouisiana State University (Baton Rouge, La.). Center of Civil Law Studies,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8215080740uhttps://law.lsu.edu/clo/digest-online/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250814123743/https://law.lsu.edu/clo/digest-online/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02355nai a22003857i wotm2008-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ne || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)6182152604aThe Peace Palace Library :bHome of International law.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aPeace Palace Library : Home of International Law 1a[The Hague] :bThe Peace Palace Library  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2008).  aFeatured between 2005-03 and 2008-10 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Library of the Peace Palace has one of the world’s largest collections in the field of international law, public and private law, and foreign national law, as well as an extensive collection on international political and diplomatic history and the history of peace movements.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aPeace Palace Library (Hague, Netherlands)vCatalogs. 0aInternational lawvBibliographyvCatalogs. 0aLawvBibliographyvCatalogs.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106726 0aInternational law & organizations 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 0aForeign & comparative law 0aInternational / multinational 6aOrganization website40uhttps://peacepalacelibrary.nl413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261016054232/https://peacepalacelibrary.nlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02994nai a22003737i wotm2009-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| d o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aMapLight.org. 1a[Berkeley, Calif.] :bMapLight  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe site’s name is an acronym for Money And Politics: Illuminating the Connection. According to the site’s About Us section: “MAPLight.org, … illuminates the connection between campaign donations and legislative votes in unprecedented ways. Elected officials collect large sums of money to run their campaigns, and they often pay back campaign contributors with special access and favorable laws. This common practice is contrary to the public interest, yet legal. MAPLight.org makes money/vote connections transparent, to help citizens hold their legislators accountable.” The database combines three data sets: Bill texts and legislative voting records; Supporting and opposing interests for each bill; and Campaign contribution data from the Center for Responsive Politics and the National Institute on Money in State Politics.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCampaign fundszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008100035 0aLobbyingzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106892 0aLegislationzUnited States. 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402608140uhttps://www.maplight.org413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261026052115/https://www.maplight.orgzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.423Comparable current resource: OpenSecretsuhttps://www.opensecrets.org/423Comparable current resource, archived version: OpenSecretsuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261110015055/https://www.opensecrets.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02135nai a22003377i wotm2009-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)3322839300aHuman Rights Brief. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bAmerican University Washington College of Law  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aHuman Rights Brief is a student-run publication of the Washington College of Law’s Center for Human Rights and Humanitarian Law. This periodical reports on developments in international human rights and humanitarian law and provides concise legal analysis of cutting edge human rights issues.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aHuman rightsvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008105911 0aInternational lawvPeriodicals. 0aHuman rights 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aInternational / multinational 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102635240uhttps://digitalcommons.wcl.american.edu/hrbrief/about.html413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260303092659/https://digitalcommons.wcl.american.edu/hrbrief/about.htmlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02666nai a22004097i wotm2009-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999txu|| w o    s0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)80930533  ae-uk-en04aThe Anglo-American Legal Tradition. 1a[Houston, Texas] :bThe O'Quinn Law Library/University of Houston Law Center  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site contains documents from Medieval and Early Modern England (1218-1650) from the National Archives in London. These documents are digitized and displayed through The O’Quinn Law Library of the University of Houston Law Center by license of the National Archives. The documents include a wide range of series from both common law, equity courts and from the exchequer.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawxHistory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075133 0aLawzEnglandxHistory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106753 0aLawzGreat BritainxHistory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075164 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aUnited Kingdom (England) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aRecords (Documents).2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261632 aUniversity of Houston.bLaw Center,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8513031540uhttp://aalt.law.uh.edu413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261021155934/http://aalt.law.uh.eduzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02465nai a22003377i wotm2009-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aNixonTapes.org. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bNixonTapes.org  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aKudos to Lyonette Louis-Jacques, the Foreign and International Law Librarian & Lecturer in Law at the University of Chicago D’Angelo Law Library, for making me aware of this month’s first site — Nixontapes.org — via one of her Twitter posts. This site contains transcripts and mp3 files of Nixon tapes made between February 1971 and July 1973 (approximately 2,150 hours and 6,000 audio files). Also included are the NARA-created tape logs and time codes, the president’s daily diary, and pertinent information about each conversation. Topics include discussions of the Watergate affair, conversations with advisers (mainly Henry Kissinger), visits to China, and domestic and foreign policy, including the Vietnam war.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aWatergate Affair, 1972-1974vSources. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf202202607940uhttps://nixontapes.org/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261027084248/https://nixontapes.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02858nai a22003977i wotm2009-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| d o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)85371321  an-us---00aOpenCongress. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aContinued by a successor resource (linked below).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThis site is a project of the Sunlight Foundation and the Participatory Politics Foundation, and describes itself as “[a]n open-source, non-partisan, legislative Web resource that uses structured data scraped from THOMAS by GovTrack.us to show legislative information – bills, committees, member profiles – in a more useable format. OpenCongress.org offers RSS feeds as an easy and convenient way to follow the latest news and blog mentions relating to a bill, a vote or a member of Congress. The site serves as a rich resource for political bloggers, issue-based membership groups, and individuals.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aUnited States.bCongress.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790068651http://isni.org/isni/0000000123226449 0aLegislationzUnited States. 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aLegislative materials.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263622 aSunlight Foundation,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200701420900tGovTrack.us423Announcement of the move to GovTrackuhttps://sunlightfoundation.com/2016/02/12/farewell-opencongress-hello-govtrack/423Successor resource: GovTrack.usuhttps://www.govtrack.us/423Successor resource, archived version: GovTrack.usuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261015044035/https://www.govtrack.us/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02912nai a22003977i wotm2009-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)71297654  an-us---00aSunlight Foundation. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bSunlight Foundation  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Sunlight Foundation was founded in 2006 with the goal of using technology to enable citizens to learn more about what their elected representatives are doing, to help reduce corruption, ensure greater transparency and accountability by government, and foster public trust in the institutions of democracy. The site features include Congressional ethics, political spending, earmarking, and watchdog information; blogs and reports monitoring Congress; grant information; and “Sunlight Seekr,” a tool using name or zip code to cross-search multiple web sites to keep tabs on Congress.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aUnited States.bCongressxEthics.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140775 0aPolitical corruptionzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85033059 0aUnited StatesxAppropriations and expenditures.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85139798 0aUnited StatesxPolitics and government.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140410 0aElections, ethics & government accountability 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aSunlight Foundation,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200701420940uhttps://sunlightfoundation.com/taxonomy/term/opencongress/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260328092355/https://sunlightfoundation.com/taxonomy/term/opencongress/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02594nai a22004097i wotm2009-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)316895044  an-us---00aRecovery.gov. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aEstablished to provide education, transparency, and accountability regarding the American Recovery and Reinvestment Act, the site provides explanations of the legislation, shows how, when and where the funds are to be spent, and provides a forum in which taxpayers may evaluate the Act’s progress and provide feedback.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aUnited States.tAmerican Recovery and Reinvestment Act of 2009.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no2009054981 0aEconomic stabilizationzUnited States. 0aFinancial crisesxGovernment policyzUnited States. 0aUnited StatesxAppropriations and expenditures, 2009.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2020005774 0aUnited StatesxAppropriations and expendituresvStatistics. 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aBusiness, tax, trade & finance 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website 6aTracker / map / dashboard1 aUnited States.bRecovery Accountability and Transparency Board,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200904873940uhttps://webarchive.library.unt.edu/web/20130213204541mp_/http://www.recovery.gov/Pages/default.aspx02607nai a22003617i wotm2009-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999xx || w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aFree Government Information. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bFree Government Information  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the homepage, “Free Government Information (FGI) is a place for initiating dialogue and building consensus among the various players (libraries, government agencies, non-profit organizations, researchers, journalists, etc.) who have a stake in the preservation of and perpetual free access to government information. FGI promotes free government information through collaboration, education, advocacy and research.” FGI was founded by and continues to be maintained by a group of librarians who volunteer their time and talent to this cause.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aGovernment informationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008105358 0aGovernment publicationszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140119 0aDepository librarieszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009123198 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website 7aBlogs.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201402605140uhttps://freegovinfo.info/node/10/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261107045033/https://freegovinfo.info/node/10/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02556nai a22004097i wotm2009-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| d o    |0    2eng d  ae-uk---ae-ie---00aBAILII :bBritish and Irish Legal Information Institute. 1a[London] :bInstitute of Advanced Legal Studies  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis site provides access to a comprehensive set of freely available British and Irish primary legal materials, including British and Irish case law and legislation, European Union case law, Law Commission reports, and other law-related British and Irish material.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzGreat Britain.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075163 0aLawzIreland.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075171 0aLaw reports, digests, etc.zGreat Britain.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008106819 0aForeign & comparative law 0aCourts, judiciary & case law 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aUnited Kingdom 5aIreland 5aEuropean Union 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aLaw materials.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20110263512 aUniversity of London.bInstitute of Advanced Legal Studies,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n5004549140uhttps://www.bailii.org/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260101043252/https://www.bailii.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03037nai a22004577i wotm2009-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)34709411  ae-uk---00aOffice of Public Sector Information. 1a[London] :bUK National Archives  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis website provides online access to UK legislation and official publications. It provides guidance on official publishing and crown copyright, information on licensing, the information asset register, and the information trade scheme. The Office of Public Sector Information (OPSI) has grown out of Her Majesty’s Stationary Office (HMSO).cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aGreat Britain.bOffice of Public Sector Information.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no2005080891 0aGovernment publicationszGreat Britain.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh88007414 0aLegislationzGreat Britain. 0aLawzGreat Britain.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075163 0aCopyrightzGreat Britain.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101747 0aGreat BritainxPolitics and governmenty1945-0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85056922 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aForeign & comparative law 0aLegislation & legislative process 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aUnited Kingdom 6aGovernment agency website1 aGreat Britain.bOffice of Public Sector Information,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20050808912 aNational Archives (Great Britain),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr200301288840uhttps://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/c/F268678413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250419215345/https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/c/F268678zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02904nai a22003137i 4500001001200000005001700012006001900029007001500048008004100063043001200104245004400116264005200160300002200212336002600234337002600260338003600286500008800322500008100410500022000491506006500711520127600776588015402052653004102206653002802247653003302275655008302308856004202391856015702433wotm2009-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999miu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---04aThe Collected Works of Abraham Lincoln. 1a[Ann Arbor, Michigan] :bUniversity of Michigan  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aIsmael Gullon, the Associate Law Librarian for Collections & Technical Services at Mercer University’s Furman Smith Law Library and the former OBS-SIS Chair who spear-headed the Website of the Month project, suggested this month’s first site: The Collected Works of Abraham Lincoln. According to the homepage, “In 1953, the Abraham Lincoln Association published The Collected Works of Abraham Lincoln, a multi-volume set of Lincoln’s correspondence, speeches, and other writings. Roy P. Basler and his editorial staff, with the continued support of the association, spent five years transcribing and annotating Lincoln’s papers. The Collected Works of Abraham Lincoln represented the first major scholarly effort to collect and publish the complete writings of Abraham Lincoln, and the edition has remained an invaluable resource to Lincoln scholars. Through the efforts of the Abraham Lincoln Association, the edition is now available in electronic form.” The site allows visitors to preform simple, boolean and proximity searches, as well as browse titles, browse through lists of all unique words in the text, and review the symbols used to describe sources as cited at the beginning of the first footnote to each item.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf202202607940uhttps://quod.lib.umich.edu/l/lincoln/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260609132830/https://quod.lib.umich.edu/l/lincoln/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02088nai a22003497i wotm2009-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ctu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)58397545  an-us---04aThe Avalon Project at Yale Law School :bThe Federalist Papers. 1a[New Haven, Connecticut] :bYale Law School  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2009).  aFeatured 2009-01 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAppropriately, this site provides the electronic text of the Federalist Papers, a collection of essays written by Alexander Hamilton, James Madison, and John Jay.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aConstitutional lawzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85139986 0aConstitutional law & civil rights 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf202202607940uhttps://avalon.law.yale.edu/subject_menus/fed.asp413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261101204341/https://avalon.law.yale.edu/subject_menus/fed.aspzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02671nai a22003617i wotm2010-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aMPI Immigration Data Hub. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bMigration Policy Institute  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAccording to the website, “The MPI Data Hub showcases in-depth and latest data on immigrant trends and patterns in the United States and around the world. Research tools include US State Data on the Foreign Born, Maps of the Foreign Born, the World Migration Map, Comparative Charts and Tables, the Global Remittances Guide, and asylum data. To date, the Data Hub has compiled stock, flow, citizenship, asylum, and historical data for 17 countries, including the United States, as well as extensive data from the US Census Bureau and Department of Homeland Security that cover the numbers and characteristics of immigrant populations residing in and arriving to the United States every year.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aEmigration and immigrationvStatistics. 0aUnited StatesxEmigration and immigrationvStatistics. 0aImmigration & citizenship 0aUnited States (federal) 0aInternational / multinational 6aTracker / map / dashboard 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261812 aMigration Policy Institute,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200303341140uhttps://www.migrationpolicy.org/content/data-hub413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260406052259/https://www.migrationpolicy.org/content/data-hubzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02795nai a22003737i wotm2010-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)61064087400aIntegrating Resources :bA Cataloging Manual - Appendix A to the BIBCO Participants' Manual and Module 35 of the CONSER Cataloging Manual.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aIntegrating Resources: A Cataloging Manual, Appendix a to the Bibco Participants’ Manual and Module 35 of the Conser Cataloging Manual. 2010 Revision 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bProgram for Cooperative Cataloging  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Integrating Resources: A Cataloging Manual was first issued in 2003 and represented a significant milestone in the development of cataloging documentation. The manual was later revised in 2005 and 2008 to incorporate new practices and changes in the technical services landscape. In 2010 guidelines for repeatable 260 field were added to section 7.3.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aBIBCO (Program)vHandbooks, manuals, etc.20aCONSER ProgramvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 0aCataloging of integrating resourcesvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 0aCooperative catalogingzUnited StatesvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261092 aProgram for Cooperative Cataloging,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9601198540uhttps://wwws.loc.gov/aba/pcc/conser/more-documentation.html413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261110210812/https://wwws.loc.gov/aba/pcc/conser/more-documentation.htmlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02645nai a22004337i wotm2010-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| w o    |0    2mul d  ae-uk---ae-fr---ae-it---00aPrimary Sources on Copyright History (1450-1900).1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aPrimary Sources on Copyright (1450-1900) 1a[Cambridge, England] :bUniversity of Cambridge  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis is a digital archive of primary sources on copyright from the invention of the printing press (c. 1450) to the Berne Convention (1886) and beyond. These include privileges, statutes, judicial decisions, contracts and materials relating to legislative history, but also contemporary letters, essays, treatises and artefacts from Italy, Germany, France, Britain and the United States, in Italian, German, French, English and Latin.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aCopyrightxHistoryvSources. 0aCopyrightzEuropexHistory. 0aIntellectual property, technology & privacy 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aForeign (single country or region) 0aUnited States (federal) 5aItaly 5aGermany 5aFrance 5aUnited Kingdom 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20220260792 aUniversity of Cambridge,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7901886240uhttps://copyrighthistory.org/cam413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260810121715/https://copyrighthistory.org/camzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02184nai a22003017i 4500001001200000005001700012006001900029007001500048008004100063245001800104264007200122300002200194336002600216337002600242338003600268500008800304500008100392500006000473500019300533506006500726520050500791588015401296650009601450650005601546653005001602653004501652856018501697wotm2010-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || w o    |0    2eng d00aEarth Portal. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Earth Portal is a comprehensive resource for timely, objective, science-based information about the environment. It is a means for the global scientific community to come together to produce the first free, expert-driven, massively scalable information resource on the environment, and to engage civil society in a public dialogue on the role of environmental issues in human affairs. It contains no commercial advertising and reaches a large global audience.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aEnvironmental sciencesvEncyclopedias.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008119801 0aEnvironmental sciencesxComputer network resources. 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites)403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20220120160907/http://www.earthportal.orgzArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02841nai a22003737i wotm2010-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ke || w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)23236006500aKick the Habit :bA UN Guide to Climate Neutrality. 1a[Nairobi, Kenya] :bUnited Nations  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aKick the Habit, is written by experts from many disciplines and various countries, with leading research organizations involved in preparing and reviewing the publication. It presents solutions, from reducing consumption and increasing energy efficiency to offsetting emissions via carbon trading schemes, for individuals, businesses, cities and countries plus other groups that have similar characteristics such as NGO and intergovernmental organizations. The book contains case studies, illustrations, maps and graphics and serves also as reference publication.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aClimatic changes.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85027037 0aCarbon dioxide mitigation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh97007879 0aGreenhouse gas mitigation.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98006982 0aGlobal warming.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh89000812 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aInternational / multinational 7aGuidebooks.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261082 aUnited Nations Environment Programme,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8000238840uhttps://www.unep.org/resources/report/kick-habit-un-guide-climate-neutrality413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260119040158/https://www.unep.org/resources/report/kick-habit-un-guide-climate-neutralityzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02540nai a22004097i wotm2010-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)55039537  an-us---00aInnocence Project. 1a[New York] :bInnocence Project  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Innocence Project was founded in 1992 by Barry C. Scheck and Peter J. Neufeld at the Benjamin N. Cardozo School of Law at Yeshiva University to assist prisoners who could be proven innocent through DNA testing. The website is organized into several components providing information on cases, wrongful convictions, and DNA evidence. Other sections provide updates on relevant criminal justice legislation and the latest DNA news.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aJudicial errorzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008122557 0aEx-convictszUnited States. 0aFalse imprisonmentzUnited States. 0aDNA fingerprintingzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009123619 0aPost-conviction remedieszUnited States. 0aCriminalszUnited StatesvIdentification. 0aCriminal law & criminal justice 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 6aOrganization website40uhttps://innocenceproject.org/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029214230/https://innocenceproject.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02258nai a22003377i wotm2010-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuudcu|| d o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aRegulatory Impact Analyses. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aCreated by the AEI-Brookings Joint Center for Regulatory Studies, this is a centralized online database of regulatory impact analyses (RIAs) and related Federal Register notices.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAdministrative procedurezUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100597 0aTrade regulationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008112738 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aAEI-Brookings Joint Center for Regulatory Studies,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nr00005430423Comparable current resource: RegInfo.gov (OIRA EO 12866 review and Unified Agenda)uhttps://reginfo.gov423Comparable current resource, archived version: RegInfo.gov (OIRA EO 12866 review and Unified Agenda)uhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250220021207/https://reginfo.govzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02631nai a22003617i wotm2010-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuilu|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us-ilan-us---00aLincoln/Net :bAbraham Lincoln Historical Digitization Project.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aLincoln/Net : Abraham Lincoln Historical Digitization Project / Northern Illinois University 1a[DeKalb, Illinois] :bNorthern Illinois University  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aPresents biographical information on and speeches and writings of U.S. President Abraham Lincoln (1809-1865), emphasizing Lincoln’s Illinois years from 1815-1861. Also provides a database of primary source materials related to antebellum life in Illinois, featuring letters, diaries, political pamphlets, songbooks, and hyperlinks to resources related to Lincoln’s political and social context. Includes discussions of eight historical themes and an online Lincoln biography.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 5aIllinois 6aDigital archive / collection 7aPrimary sources.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20220260792 aNorthern Illinois University,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79088908403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250318104612/https://digital.lib.niu.edu/islandora/object/niu-lincoln%3AcollectionzArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02805nai a22004097i wotm2010-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)65639907  an-us---00aProject on Emerging Nanotechnologies. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bWoodrow Wilson International Center for Scholars  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe Project on Emerging Nanotechnologies was established in April 2005 as a partnership between the Woodrow Wilson International Center for Scholars and the Pew Charitable Trusts. The Project is dedicated to helping ensure that as nanotechnologies advance, possible risks are minimized, public and consumer engagement remains strong, and the potential benefits of these new technologies are realized.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aNanotechnology.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh91001490 0aNanotechnologyxResearch.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2014002668 0aNanotechnologyxEnvironmental aspects. 0aNanotechnologyxLaw and legislationzUnited States. 0aIntellectual property, technology & privacy 0aHealth, disability & social welfare 0aUnited States (federal) 6aOrganization website2 aWoodrow Wilson International Center for Scholars,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n780863972 aPew Charitable Trusts,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8606555840uhttps://www.wilsoncenter.org/publication-series/project-emerging-nanotechnologies413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260901081619/https://www.wilsoncenter.org/publication-series/project-emerging-nanotechnologieszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02763nai a22004217i wotm2010-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)300300431  an-us---04aThe White House :bPresident George W. Bush. 1aWashington, D.C :bU.S. National Archives and Records Administration  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aTitle, publication and subject data from the University of Hawaiʻi Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe official web site for President George W. Bush, the 43rd President of the United States. This site is a source for information about the President, Vice President, First Lady, Mrs. Cheney, and policies of the Bush Administration. “This is historical material, ‘frozen in time.’ The web site is no longer updated and links to external web sites and some internal pages will not work.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPresidentszUnited StatesvBiography. 0aSelective dissemination of informationzUnited States. 0aUnited StatesxPolitics and governmenty2001-2009. 0aUnited StatesxHistoryy21st century. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website 6aDigital archive / collection1 aUnited States.bPresident (2001-2009 : Bush),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20010207711 aUnited States.bNational Archives and Records Administration,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8417610140uhttps://georgewbush-whitehouse.archives.gov/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261024005541/https://georgewbush-whitehouse.archives.gov/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02819nai a22003257i wotm2010-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999wiu|| w o    s0    2eng d  an-us---04aThe J. Willard Hurst Collection (1932-1997). 1a[Madison, Wisconsin] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2010).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis online collection, created by the University of Wisconsin Law Library, details the career of the man commonly identified as the father of modern American legal history. The collection primarily spans the years 1932 through Hurst’s death in 1997. Most of the material dates between 1946 and 1980, when Hurst was a professor at the University of Wisconsin Law School, where he developed the field of American legal economic history through his scholarship and teaching. The collection provides insight into the evolution of Hurst’s view of legal history and his role in developing a community for legal historians. It includes Hurst’s personal outlines and notes, course texts, publications, publication reviews, research notes, correspondence (incoming and carbon copies of outgoing letters), personnel records, photographs, audio recordings, and even his personal typewriter. Correspondence, topical outlines and notes, and audio recordings compose the bulk of the collection.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzUnited StatesxHistoriography. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 6aDigital archive / collection2 aUniversity of Wisconsin--Madison.bLaw Library,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no201904573240uhttps://repository.law.wisc.edu/s/uwlaw/page/hurst413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260904022055/https://repository.law.wisc.edu/s/uwlaw/page/hurstzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02627nai a22003497i wotm2011-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999vau|| w o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aGovernment Information Resources :bAdministrative Decisions & Other Actions. 1a[Charlottesville, Virginia] :bUniversity of Virginia Library  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aCreated by the University of Virginia Library, this website is an online directory to decisions and other legal actions issued by federal agencies of the United States. The directory can be viewed A-Z by agency or by subject. According to the website, “This page is not an attempt to link to Federal Register or the Code of Federal Regulations information for each federal agency. It links to other administrative actions which are outside the scope of the CFR or the FR. What is available via the Internet varies from agency to agency.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aAdministrative lawzUnited StatesvCases.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100632 0aAdministrative agencieszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2007100596 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 6aResearch guide (web)2 aUniversity of Virginia.bLibrary,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7912789540uhttps://guides.lib.virginia.edu/administrative_decisions413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20200913164226/https://guides.lib.virginia.edu/administrative_decisionszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03144nai a22003617i wotm2011-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuutxu|| d o    |0    2eng d00a18thConnect :bEighteenth-Century Scholarship Online.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:a18Thconnect 1a[College Station, Tex.] :bCenter of Digital Humanities Research  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.  aThis site is an aggregator of digital resources that provide a comprehensive research environment for scholars working on the literature, history, the fine arts, and philosophy of the long eighteenth century (1660-1800). According to the website, “Our main concerns are: Access via plain-text searching for all scholars to open access and proprietary and digital archives including EEBO and ECCO even if their institutions are unable to afford those resources; Peer- review of the growing number of digital resources and archives for which 18thConnect offers an online finding aid; Reflection on Best Practices with scholars who are negotiating new modes of publication and scholarly production.”cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aEighteenth century.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85041401 0aEnglish literaturex18th centuryxHistory and criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008102755 0aGeneral reference (not law-specific) 0aLegal history & historical documents 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites) 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aTexas A & M University,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n80125885403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20240812201242/https://18thconnect.org/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.423Comparable current resource: ECCO-TCP texts (Oxford Text Archive)uhttps://llds.ling-phil.ox.ac.uk/llds/xmlui/handle/20.500.14106/7423Comparable current resource, archived version: ECCO-TCP texts (Oxford Text Archive)uhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260804142117/https://llds.ling-phil.ox.ac.uk/llds/xmlui/handle/20.500.14106/7zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02755nai a22003737i wotm2011-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuflu|| d o    |0    2eng d  an-us---00aNCSTL.org. 1a[Gulfport, Fla.] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aOriginal site no longer available (checked 2026-11-10).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe National Clearinghouse for Science, Technology and the Law is hosted by Stetson University College of Law. It is a program of the National Institute of Justice, Office of Justice Programs, United States Department of Justice. The website includes searchable comprehensive bibliography on law, science and technology. The forensic database contains court decisions and commentary, scholarly publications, commercial applications, professional associations and institutions, and other resources about traditional and new forensic topics.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aForensic scienceszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008121040 0aEvidence, ExpertzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008103258 0aScience and law.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85118618 0aCriminal law & criminal justice 0aIntellectual property, technology & privacy 0aUnited States (federal) 7aBibliographies.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026048 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aStetson University.bCollege of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n50053198403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250428231041/http://www.ncstl.org/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02529nai a22003737i wotm2011-0420261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ohu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)69779480300aPerceptions of Libraries, 2010 :bContext and Community, a Report to the OCLC Membership. 1a[Dublin, Ohio] :bOCLC  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aOCLC first published the “Perceptions of libraries and information resources” in 2005. The new report provides updated information and new insights into information consumers and their online habits, preferences, and perceptions. Particular attention was paid to how the current economic downturn has affected the information-seeking behaviors and how those changes are reflected in the use and perception of libraries.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLibrariesxPublic opinion. 0aLibrary usersxAttitudes. 0aLibrariesxUser satisfactionvStatistics. 0aLibrary use studies.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85076741 0aLibrary surveys.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85076739 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 6aReport or study (single document)2 aOCLC,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7801529440uhttps://www.oclc.org/research/publications/2010.html413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260610121053/https://www.oclc.org/research/publications/2010.htmlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02863nai a22003257i wotm2011-0520261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    |0    2eng d00aMARC Record Guide for Monograph Aggregator Vendors - Second Edition.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aMarc Record Guide for Monograph Aggregators 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bLibrary of Congress  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis was featured in a post to the TSLL Tech Scan list on March 18. AALL’s own Yael Mandelstam and George Prager are among the co-authors. Here is the post to the TSLL Tech Scans Blog: From a message by Ms. Kate Harcourt, Director for Original and Special Materials Cataloging at Columbia University, sent to the OCLC Cataloging list on March 10: “The Program for Cooperative Cataloging published a guide for vendors. I think vendors will only improve the quality of records if we insist on better records. Please share this guide with your vendors as it maps out in detail how to construct a good quality MARC record. This is the second edition, updated in fall 2010. Yael Mandelstam and George Prager are among the four authors. Maybe we all should send the guide to the legal publishers who produce record sets!cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aMARC formats.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85080966 0aCataloging of electronic books.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh95004295 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261092 aProgram for Cooperative Cataloging,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9601198540uhttps://www.loc.gov/aba/pcc/sca/documents/FinalVendorGuide.pdf413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20100608070212/http://www.loc.gov/catdir/pcc/sca/FinalVendorGuide.pdfzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03208nai a22003737i wotm2011-0620261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)705389114  an-us---00aWomen in America :bIndicators of Social and Economic Well-Being. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bU.S. Department of Commerce Economics and Statistics Administration  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aIn support of the Council on Women and Girls, the Office of Management and Budget and the Economics and Statistics Administration within the Department of Commerce worked together to create this report which, for the first time in recent history, pulls together information from across the Federal statistical agencies to compile baseline information on how women are faring in the United States today and how these trends have changed over time. The report provides a statistical portrait showing how women?s lives are changing in five critical areas: People, Families, and Income; Education; Employment; Health; Crime and Violence. This is the first such federal initiative since 1963, when the Commission on Status of Women, established by President Kennedy and chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt, produced a report on the conditions of women. In addition to the report, the White House website also provides additional resources related to women’s economic and social status today.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aWomenzUnited StatesxSocial conditionsvStatistics. 0aWomenzUnited StatesxEconomic conditionsvStatistics. 0aGender, sexuality, family & children 0aUnited States (federal) 6aReport or study (single document) 7aStatistics.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261811 aUnited States.bEconomics and Statistics Administration,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no9100261740uhttps://www.census.gov/library/publications/2011/demo/womeninamerica.html413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260922225138/https://www.census.gov/library/publications/2011/demo/womeninamerica.htmlzBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02549nai a22003377i wotm2011-0720261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999miu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)31853575300aHathiTrust Digital Library.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aHathitrust 1a[Ann Arbor, Mich.] :bHathiTrust  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aAs a digital repository for the nation’s great research libraries, HathiTrust brings together the immense collections of partner institutions. It was initially conceived as a collaboration of the thirteen universities of the Committee on Institutional Cooperation, the University of California system, and the University of Virginia to establish a repository for those universities to archive and share their digitized collections, and quickly expanded to include additional partners with fast growing treasure of digitized collections. As shown on the visualization of HathiTrust works by call number page (http://www.hathitrust.org/visualizations_callnumbers), 22% of the works are classified in KF.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aDigital libraries.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh95008857 0aElectronic books.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh93007047 0aLaw librarianship, cataloging & information management 6aDigital archive / collection2 aHathiTrust,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no201404277340uhttps://www.hathitrust.org/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260731173144/https://www.hathitrust.org/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02927nai a22003857i wotm2011-0820261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuune || w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)25564730604aThe Hague justice portal. 1aHague, Netherlands :bThe Hague  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aTitle, publication and subject data from the University of Hawaiʻi Law Library catalog record.  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aLaunched in 2006, the Hague Justice Portal (Portail Judiciaire de La Haye) was created by The Hague Academic Coalition to provide a virtual gateway to news, research materials, and general information pertaining to The Hague’s role in international peace, justice, and security. Designed to improve access to the Hague courts and encourage academic debate, the portals main projects include the Hague Justice Journal (requires subscription), the PCA Awards Project (with the Permanent Court of Arbitration), and the DomCLIC project (Domestic Jurisprudence on International Criminal Law). The “International Justice Forum” section contains a series of interactive forums designed to facilitate discussion on topics related to international law.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aPeace.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85098940 0aJustice.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85071118 0aInternational law.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85067417 0aHague (Netherlands)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n79032987 0aInternational law & organizations 0aInternational criminal law & transitional justice 0aInternational / multinational 6aPortal or gateway (links to other sites)403Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20250104152113/http://www.haguejusticeportal.net/zArchived copy (Internet Archive Wayback Machine); the original site is no longer available.02295nai a22003377i wotm2011-0920261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110duuuuuuuuxx || d o    |0    2eng d00aFree Full-text Online Law Review/Law Journal Search Engine. 1a[Place of publication not identified] :b[publisher not identified]  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aNo verified current address for the original site could be found.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis search engine searches the free full-text of over 400 online law reviews and law journals, as well as document repositories hosting academic papers and related publications such as Congressional Research Service reports. Several of the law reviews and legal journals, working papers, and reports are available online only.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawvPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85075138 0aLawxComputer network resources. 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026081 7aLaw reviews.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026352423Comparable current resource: Law Review Commonsuhttps://lawreviewcommons.com/423Comparable current resource, archived version: Law Review Commonsuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261027194837/https://lawreviewcommons.com/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03582nai a22004337i wotm2011-1020261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cau|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)41306389  an-us---00aNolo's Legal Encyclopedia.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aFree Legal Information and Solutions, Also Known as Nolo’s Legal Encyclopedia 1a[Berkeley, Calif.] :bNOLO  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011, 2022).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aFeatured between 2022-04 and 2022-08 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aTitle, publication and subject data from the University of Hawaiʻi Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis Nolo site presents an online legal encyclopedia of free legal articles and other materials. Major topics include: accidents & injuries; bankruptcy; business, LLCs & corporations; criminal law; divorce & family law; DUI/DWI & traffic tickets; employment law; immigration; nonprofits; patents, copyright & trademark; personal finance & retirement; real estate & rental property; small claims court & lawsuits; taxes; wills, trusts & estates. Also link to the Nolo’s Plain-English Law Dictionary and selected free online books.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aLegal encyclopedia Website provides free legal articles and legal updates such as a new critical U. S. Supreme Court decision on search-and-seizure rights. Major topics include: accidents & injuries; bankruptcy; business, LLCs & corporations; criminal law; divorce & family law; DUI/DWI & traffic tickets; employment law; immigration; nonprofits; patents, copyright & trademark; personal finance & retirement; real estate & rental property; small claims court & lawsuits; taxes; wills, trusts & estates. Also includes information on doing legal research, podcasts, Nolo’s Plain-English Law Dictionary, a financial calculator, and selected free online books.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLawzUnited StatesvEncyclopedias. 0aLawzUnited StatesvDictionaries. 0aLegal researchvEncyclopedias. 0aLegal research & reference tools 0aLegal profession, education & access to justice 0aUnited States (federal) 0aUnited States (state, local or multi-state) 7aEncyclopedias.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260922 aNolo (Firm),eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n200109452340uhttps://www.nolo.com/legal-encyclopedia413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260630132658/https://www.nolo.com/legal-encyclopediazBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02912nai a22003737i wotm2011-1120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999nyu|| w o    i0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)29886237700aUniversal Declaration of Human Rights (1948) :bDrafting History.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aThe Universal Declaration of Human Rights: An Historical Record of the Drafting Process 1a[New York] :bUnited Nations  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis website provides access to United Nations documentation related to the drafting of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. From 1946-1948 delegates to the United Nations discussed and drafted an international declaration on the subject of human rights that has become a standard of principles for human rights. The Universal Declaration of Human Rights was adopted by General Assembly resolution 217A at its 3rd session in Paris on 10 December 1948. This website presents documents in chronological order, arranged according to the various bodies that met to discuss, draft and re-draft the Declaration. There are also brief biographic notes for the members of the Drafting Committee formed by the UN Commission on Human Rights.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.20aUnited Nations.bGeneral Assembly.tUniversal Declaration of Human Rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n81139937 0aHuman rights.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85026379 0aHuman rights 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aInternational / multinational 6aDigital archive / collection 7aLegislative histories.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102636140uhttps://research.un.org/en/undhr/draftingcommittee413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261029045937/https://research.un.org/en/undhr/draftingcommitteezBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.03221nai a22003977i wotm2011-1220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999dcu|| w o    f0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)37622946  an-us---00aFederal Labor Relations Authority. 1a[Washington, D.C.] :bUnited States Federal Labor Relations Authority  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2011).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe FLRA is an independent agency responsible for administering the labor-management relations program for federal employees world-wide. The site features full-text Authority cases from 1971 to the present and Impasse Panel Final Actions dating back to 1990. Includes information regarding FLRA’s processes in dealing with unfair labor practices, representation issues, arbitration appeals, and negotiation disputes; addresses and phone numbers of Regional Offices; Authority decisions; Closed court Litigation decisions; Office of the General Counsel policies and guidance; information regarding the agency’s Collaboration and Alternative Dispute Resolution (CADR) activities; press releases; the FLRA Bulletin; and biographies of the Authority Chair and Members, the General Counsel and the Panel Members.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger.10aUnited States.bFederal Labor Relations Authority.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n791040641http://isni.org/isni/0000000121079262 0aEmployee-management relations in governmentxLaw and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008103013 0aLabor laws and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85073707 0aCollective bargainingxGovernment employeeszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101173 0aLabor & employment 0aGovernment information & administrative law 0aUnited States (federal) 6aGovernment agency website1 aUnited States.bFederal Labor Relations Authority,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7910406440uhttps://www.flra.gov/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261017134857/https://www.flra.gov/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02753nai a22003737i wotm2012-0120261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999enk|| d o    |0    2eng d  ae-uk-en04aThe Proceedings of the Old Bailey, 1674-1913.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aThe Proceedings of the Old Bailey, London 1674 to 1913 1a[Sheffield] :bUniversity of Sheffield  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2012).  aFeatured 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThis project is a collaboration between the Universities of Hertfordshire and Sheffield and the Open University. The site contains fully searchable texts detailing accounts of over 197,000 criminal trials held at London’s Central Criminal Court. The crimes tried were mostly felonies (predominantly theft), but also include some of the most serious misdemeanours, providing historical insight into the daily lives of those who participated in the proceedings.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aLegal history & historical documents 0aCriminal law & criminal justice 0aForeign (single country or region) 5aUnited Kingdom (England) 7aTrial and arbitral proceedings.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026708 7aDatabases.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140260812 aUniversity of Sheffield,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n790727652 aUniversity of Hertfordshire,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n9606327740uhttps://www.oldbaileyonline.org/#:~:text=A%20fully%20searchable%20edition%20of,the%20lives%20of%20executed%20convicts413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20261016135944/https://www.oldbaileyonline.org/#:~:text=A%20fully%20searchable%20edition%20of,the%20lives%20of%20executed%20convictszBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02994nai a22004097i wotm2012-0220261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999cou|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)789673142  an-us---an-usp--04aThe David H. Getches Collection.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aDavid H. Getches Collection, Also Known as the David H. Getches Digital Archive 1a[Boulder, Colo.] :bUniversity of Colorado Law School  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2012).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aMachine-assigned by Claude (Anthropic), November 2026: subject headings, name headings, geographic area codes, place of publication, 008 codes, access note. Name, subject and code values were checked against id.loc.gov; not reviewed by a cataloger.0 aUnrestricted online accessfUnrestricted online access2star  aThe University of Colorado Law Library created this digital collection in memory of the late Colorado Law School Dean David Getches. A renowned scholar in the fields of natural resources, water, and American Indian law, Getches served as Dean and Raphael J. Moses Professor of Natural Resources Law from July, 2003-June, 2011. The David H. Getches Collection at the William A. Wise Law Library is dedicated to preserving and sharing Dean Getches’ tremendous legal and educational legacy, as reflected in his scholarship, academic speeches, congressional testimony, and litigation.cLSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month  aDescription based on the LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month archive entry; site address verified 2026-11-10; resource not examined by the cataloger. 0aIndians of North AmericaxLegal status, laws, etc.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85065315 0aWater rightszWest (U.S.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008113402 0aNatural resourcesxLaw and legislationzUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008108338 0aEnvironmental, energy & natural resources law 0aIndigenous peoples & tribal law 0aLegal scholarship & law journals 0aUnited States (federal) 0aTribal / Indigenous nations 6aDigital archive / collection2 aUniversity of Colorado Boulder.bSchool of Law,eissuing body.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n8812170440uhttps://scholar.law.colorado.edu/david-h-getches/413Archived versionuhttps://web.archive.org/web/20260114233853/https://scholar.law.colorado.edu/david-h-getches/zBackup copy in the Internet Archive Wayback Machine.02613nai a22003617i wotm2012-0320261110224125.0m     o  d        cr |n|||||||||261110cuuuu9999ilu|| w o    |0    2eng d  a(OCoLC)77245955200aGenre/Form Terms for Legal Materials.1 iTitle as listed by LSRD-SIS:aGenre/Form Terms for Law Materials 1a[Chicago] :bLibrary of Congress  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  aSelected as an LSRD-SIS Legal Website of the Month (section archive listing: 2012).  aFeatured between 2009-01 and 2012-06 (estimated from dated archive sources).  aSubject headings from the University of Colorado Law Library catalog record.  a